1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,170
♫ In an optimistic future

2
00:00:03,170 --> 00:00:06,221
♫ Next Sunday A.D.

3
00:00:06,221 --> 00:00:09,623
♫ There was a guy named Joel

4
00:00:09,623 --> 00:00:12,856
♫ Not too different from you or me

5
00:00:12,856 --> 00:00:15,855
♫ He worked at Gizmonics Institute

6
00:00:15,855 --> 00:00:18,982
♫ Just another face in a red jumpsuit

7
00:00:18,982 --> 00:00:21,883
♫ He did a good job cleaning up the place

8
00:00:21,883 --> 00:00:23,583
♫ But his bosses didn't like him

9
00:00:23,583 --> 00:00:27,416
♫ So they shot him into space

10
00:00:28,526 --> 00:00:31,434
♫ We'll send him cheesy movies

11
00:00:31,434 --> 00:00:34,691
♫ The worst we can find (la-la-la)

12
00:00:34,691 --> 00:00:37,415
♫ He'll have to sit and watch them all

13
00:00:37,415 --> 00:00:40,821
♫ And we'll monitor his mind (la-la-la)

14
00:00:40,821 --> 00:00:43,750
♫ Now keep in mind Joel can't control

15
00:00:43,750 --> 00:00:47,062
♫ Where the movies begin or end (la-la-la)

16
00:00:47,062 --> 00:00:49,888
♫ Because he used those special parts

17
00:00:49,888 --> 00:00:53,555
♫ To make his robot friends

18
00:00:55,271 --> 00:00:56,880
♫ Robot Roll Call: (Come on, let's go)

19
00:00:56,880 --> 00:00:58,113
♫ Cambot (Pan left)

20
00:00:58,113 --> 00:00:59,584
♫ Gypsy (Hi girl)

21
00:00:59,584 --> 00:01:01,293
♫ Tom Servo (What a cool guy)

22
00:01:01,293 --> 00:01:03,026
♫ Croooow (You little wisecracker)

23
00:01:03,026 --> 00:01:05,724
♫ If you're wondering
how he eats and breathes

24
00:01:05,724 --> 00:01:08,812
♫ And other science facts (la-la-la)

25
00:01:08,812 --> 00:01:11,744
♫ Then repeat to
yourself, it's just a show

26
00:01:11,744 --> 00:01:15,315
♫ I should really just relax

27
00:01:15,315 --> 00:01:19,482
♫ For Mystery Science Theater 3000 ♫

28
00:01:21,568 --> 00:01:24,485
(mechanical noise)

29
00:01:29,340 --> 00:01:33,090
- Oh, blergh, yuck, it's
so cold in my mouth,

30
00:01:34,209 --> 00:01:36,838
and it tastes like it might be Cabernet.

31
00:01:36,838 --> 00:01:38,724
- Hey, kiddo, that's good stuff, come on!

32
00:01:38,724 --> 00:01:40,569
- Yeah, it's got one
quarter cleansing cream.

33
00:01:40,569 --> 00:01:41,402
- Yeah!

34
00:01:41,402 --> 00:01:42,790
- Now, that's dumb (cries).

35
00:01:42,790 --> 00:01:43,646
- Hey, everybody.

36
00:01:43,646 --> 00:01:44,806
It's a bad day around here.

37
00:01:44,806 --> 00:01:47,682
It's annual Wash and Wax Day,
the most dreaded day of all.

38
00:01:47,682 --> 00:01:49,488
You can't go near Joel
or he'll scrub you up

39
00:01:49,488 --> 00:01:50,681
to a pink pulp!

40
00:01:50,681 --> 00:01:52,151
- Oh, hi, everybody.

41
00:01:52,151 --> 00:01:53,598
Welcome to the SOL.

42
00:01:53,598 --> 00:01:55,224
It's really lucky you happened by.

43
00:01:55,224 --> 00:01:57,226
It's our annual Wash and Wax Day.

44
00:01:57,226 --> 00:02:00,916
It's one of the funnest days of all!

45
00:02:00,916 --> 00:02:02,809
- Okay, now, Tom, if you can hear me,

46
00:02:02,809 --> 00:02:04,335
you'd want to close your mouth.

47
00:02:04,335 --> 00:02:06,179
The buffers are coming by!

48
00:02:06,179 --> 00:02:08,289
- Isn't it horrifying?

49
00:02:08,289 --> 00:02:09,233
- Bl-bl-bl-blr!

50
00:02:09,233 --> 00:02:11,340
- Okay, Tom, you're almost done.

51
00:02:11,340 --> 00:02:12,940
I need Crow T. Robot.

52
00:02:12,940 --> 00:02:15,583
Okay, Crow T. Robot, where are you?

53
00:02:15,583 --> 00:02:18,000
- You'll never take me alive!

54
00:02:18,858 --> 00:02:21,441
(upbeat music)

55
00:02:24,125 --> 00:02:28,090
♫ Glibby glob, glibbly glob a
du bee low low low low low ♫

56
00:02:28,090 --> 00:02:29,636
(laughs) Boy, I feel great!

57
00:02:29,636 --> 00:02:31,053
That was just wonderful!

58
00:02:31,053 --> 00:02:33,184
Hey, who wants to go for a walk?

59
00:02:33,184 --> 00:02:35,724
♫ Red boys are delicious, delicious

60
00:02:35,724 --> 00:02:37,748
♫ Candy-colored love ♫

61
00:02:37,748 --> 00:02:39,004
- Shut up! Shut up!

62
00:02:39,004 --> 00:02:40,111
Joel, make him stop!

63
00:02:40,111 --> 00:02:41,255
- I'm sorry, your what hurts?

64
00:02:41,255 --> 00:02:43,595
- Oh, come on, Crow, take it easy.

65
00:02:43,595 --> 00:02:44,580
You made it through.

66
00:02:44,580 --> 00:02:45,959
You're going to be okay.

67
00:02:45,959 --> 00:02:47,649
Come on, I'll give you a Zagnut bar

68
00:02:47,649 --> 00:02:49,208
if you can simmer down.

69
00:02:49,208 --> 00:02:50,481
- No!

70
00:02:50,481 --> 00:02:51,565
- How about another Nutter Butter

71
00:02:51,565 --> 00:02:53,079
peanut butter sandwich cookie?

72
00:02:53,079 --> 00:02:54,300
- No!

73
00:02:54,300 --> 00:02:56,617
- Well, what do I have to
do to make it all better?

74
00:02:56,617 --> 00:02:58,516
- I want you to beat up Tom!

75
00:02:58,516 --> 00:03:01,168
- Oh, hey, you've got your
hands full with that one, huh?

76
00:03:01,168 --> 00:03:02,254
Well, gotta go!

77
00:03:02,254 --> 00:03:03,761
♫ Give me a head with hair

78
00:03:03,761 --> 00:03:06,288
♫ Long, beautiful hair ♫

79
00:03:06,288 --> 00:03:07,273
- Tom, come back here.

80
00:03:07,273 --> 00:03:08,777
The Mads are calling.

81
00:03:08,777 --> 00:03:09,610
- Yeah.

82
00:03:09,610 --> 00:03:10,443
- Huh? What?

83
00:03:10,443 --> 00:03:11,276
- Sail on, Servo.

84
00:03:11,276 --> 00:03:12,971
I love a robot with panache.

85
00:03:12,971 --> 00:03:14,519
- Yeah, right, whatever.

86
00:03:14,519 --> 00:03:16,655
Well, Joel, everyone knows that design

87
00:03:16,655 --> 00:03:19,355
is the combination of
two separate elements.

88
00:03:19,355 --> 00:03:21,619
That's why we've taken interior design

89
00:03:21,619 --> 00:03:23,779
and matched it with household pests

90
00:03:23,779 --> 00:03:26,069
and come up with something we like to call

91
00:03:26,069 --> 00:03:28,032
Decorator Roaches.

92
00:03:28,032 --> 00:03:29,569
- Yes, roaches.

93
00:03:29,569 --> 00:03:32,267
Fashions come and go,
but roaches are forever.

94
00:03:32,267 --> 00:03:36,237
Our invention exchange this
week is Swatch Roaches.

95
00:03:36,237 --> 00:03:39,040
Now for you southwest
enthusiasts, we have this

96
00:03:39,040 --> 00:03:42,045
little number I like to call La Cucaracha.

97
00:03:42,045 --> 00:03:43,877
(laughs) Get it?

98
00:03:43,877 --> 00:03:44,929
Of course you do.

99
00:03:44,929 --> 00:03:47,113
And for the sports
enthusiast in your life,

100
00:03:47,113 --> 00:03:50,308
we have the 49ers roach,
complete with colors.

101
00:03:50,308 --> 00:03:53,596
And over here, we have
the Peter Max roach.

102
00:03:53,596 --> 00:03:57,388
- Hey, I found a roach we
haven't categorized yet.

103
00:03:57,388 --> 00:03:59,922
Purple and gold, and
it's got a little skimpy

104
00:03:59,922 --> 00:04:01,146
mustache on it.

105
00:04:01,146 --> 00:04:03,109
- My God, you found the Prince roach!

106
00:04:03,109 --> 00:04:05,927
Frank, sign him up for
Penny of the Month Club.

107
00:04:05,927 --> 00:04:07,513
Say, I didn't catch your name.

108
00:04:07,513 --> 00:04:08,629
- Uh, Steve.

109
00:04:08,629 --> 00:04:09,462
Steve Reeves.

110
00:04:09,462 --> 00:04:10,422
- Steve Reeves?

111
00:04:10,422 --> 00:04:11,866
- Steve Hercules Reeves?

112
00:04:11,866 --> 00:04:12,709
Wow!

113
00:04:12,709 --> 00:04:14,137
- Frank!

114
00:04:14,137 --> 00:04:16,286
Say, you're not going to believe this.

115
00:04:16,286 --> 00:04:18,074
Talk about serendipitous experiences.

116
00:04:18,074 --> 00:04:20,062
We're showing one of your movies today.

117
00:04:20,062 --> 00:04:20,895
- Nu-uh!

118
00:04:20,895 --> 00:04:21,855
- Well, uh-huh!

119
00:04:21,855 --> 00:04:22,756
- Oh, that's great.

120
00:04:22,756 --> 00:04:25,391
I'm glad you're all happy
about the Prince roach.

121
00:04:25,391 --> 00:04:26,829
Look, I'm just going to cut out of here.

122
00:04:26,829 --> 00:04:28,327
I'll bill you for all the work, all right?

123
00:04:28,327 --> 00:04:30,027
- Oh, no, no, no, no, no, no!

124
00:04:30,027 --> 00:04:33,339
Joel, why don't you go on
with your Invention Exchange?

125
00:04:33,339 --> 00:04:36,199
- Well, sirs, our Invention Exchange

126
00:04:36,199 --> 00:04:37,616
is the Steve-o-meter.

127
00:04:37,616 --> 00:04:38,951
- No relation to Steve Reeves.

128
00:04:38,951 --> 00:04:39,784
- Right.

129
00:04:39,784 --> 00:04:40,769
Well, Steve Allen, as you know,

130
00:04:40,769 --> 00:04:43,460
is the author of over 300
books and short stories.

131
00:04:43,460 --> 00:04:44,810
- Over 4,000 pop songs.

132
00:04:44,810 --> 00:04:46,205
- The board game, Blow Your Own Horn.

133
00:04:46,205 --> 00:04:47,622
- Yeah, there are so many
things that Steve Allen

134
00:04:47,622 --> 00:04:48,455
has thought of.

135
00:04:48,455 --> 00:04:50,351
That's why we came up
with the Steve-o-meter.

136
00:04:50,351 --> 00:04:51,666
- There is the world that is known.

137
00:04:51,666 --> 00:04:52,753
There is the unknown.

138
00:04:52,753 --> 00:04:54,869
And there is what Steve knows.

139
00:04:54,869 --> 00:04:55,792
- Right, exactly.

140
00:04:55,792 --> 00:04:58,054
So, what you do is if you
thought of a new idea,

141
00:04:58,054 --> 00:04:59,653
you run the Steve-o-meter over it,

142
00:04:59,653 --> 00:05:02,685
and if it buzzes, well,
Steve's already thought of it.

143
00:05:02,685 --> 00:05:04,329
What have you got for us here, Crow?

144
00:05:04,329 --> 00:05:05,198
- Oh, okay.

145
00:05:05,198 --> 00:05:08,528
It's an extremely simple and
economical desalinization

146
00:05:08,528 --> 00:05:09,813
process for seawater.

147
00:05:09,813 --> 00:05:10,646
- That's something new.

148
00:05:10,646 --> 00:05:11,984
- Oh, okay, let's run the
Steve-o-meter over it.

149
00:05:11,984 --> 00:05:13,189
(electronic music)

150
00:05:13,189 --> 00:05:14,685
Oh, no, he's thought--

151
00:05:14,685 --> 00:05:15,518
- Oh, rats!

152
00:05:15,518 --> 00:05:16,351
- Of it already.

153
00:05:16,351 --> 00:05:17,184
- Well, how about this, Joel?

154
00:05:17,184 --> 00:05:19,724
A series of novels about
me and Jayne Meadows

155
00:05:19,724 --> 00:05:21,178
solving murders together!

156
00:05:21,178 --> 00:05:22,037
- Hmm, let's run this.

157
00:05:22,037 --> 00:05:22,870
(electronic music)

158
00:05:22,870 --> 00:05:23,703
Oh, I'm sorry.

159
00:05:23,703 --> 00:05:24,616
- How does it do that?

160
00:05:24,616 --> 00:05:26,679
- Well, here's my invention, my idea.

161
00:05:26,679 --> 00:05:27,737
It's the Steve-o-meter.

162
00:05:27,737 --> 00:05:30,205
I'll just run the Steve-o-meter
over the Steve-o-meter.

163
00:05:30,205 --> 00:05:31,038
(electronic music)

164
00:05:31,038 --> 00:05:32,610
Oh, no, he's thought of that, too!

165
00:05:32,610 --> 00:05:34,114
He's everywhere!

166
00:05:34,114 --> 00:05:35,284
He's everywhere!

167
00:05:35,284 --> 00:05:36,844
He's everywhere!

168
00:05:36,844 --> 00:05:38,145
- That's so great, Steve.

169
00:05:38,145 --> 00:05:39,465
I really appreciate that.

170
00:05:39,465 --> 00:05:42,777
You are one cool breed
of cat, let me tell you.

171
00:05:42,777 --> 00:05:45,439
Hey, Steve, check this out, huh?

172
00:05:45,439 --> 00:05:47,793
Roach burial, huh? (laughs)

173
00:05:47,793 --> 00:05:49,217
- Ooh, why, you, little...

174
00:05:49,217 --> 00:05:50,050
Ooh! Ooh!

175
00:05:53,298 --> 00:05:54,713
Talk about the movie.

176
00:05:54,713 --> 00:05:55,797
- Oh, all right.

177
00:05:55,797 --> 00:05:58,130
This is the first or second?

178
00:05:58,990 --> 00:05:59,823
- [Voiceover] Second.

179
00:05:59,823 --> 00:06:01,522
- This is the second movie that I did,

180
00:06:01,522 --> 00:06:02,824
Hercules Unchained.

181
00:06:02,824 --> 00:06:05,202
It's a much younger Steve Reeves.

182
00:06:05,202 --> 00:06:07,306
And let me tell you, on this set,

183
00:06:07,306 --> 00:06:09,121
I toasted more than one brain cell,

184
00:06:09,121 --> 00:06:11,173
if you know what I'm saying.

185
00:06:11,173 --> 00:06:13,291
- [Voiceover] Push the button.

186
00:06:13,291 --> 00:06:14,603
- All right, push the button.

187
00:06:14,603 --> 00:06:15,756
Here you go.

188
00:06:15,756 --> 00:06:18,826
- Movie sign, Steve Allen
thought of that, too!

189
00:06:18,826 --> 00:06:20,950
(loud screaming)

190
00:06:20,950 --> 00:06:23,867
(mechanical noise)

191
00:06:29,874 --> 00:06:30,707
- Hmm, hmm, hmm.

192
00:06:30,707 --> 00:06:31,540
- Oh, looking interesting.

193
00:06:31,540 --> 00:06:33,035
Hmm, hmm.

194
00:06:33,035 --> 00:06:35,041
- Lux Films, for dishes.

195
00:06:35,041 --> 00:06:36,041
- Compagnie.

196
00:06:37,975 --> 00:06:40,808
- Steve Reeves and The Vandellas.

197
00:06:40,808 --> 00:06:42,343
- Steve Allen thought of that.

198
00:06:42,343 --> 00:06:43,176
- OH.

199
00:06:43,176 --> 00:06:44,097
- Unchained Hercules.

200
00:06:44,097 --> 00:06:47,664
♫ Oh, Hercules, my darling ♫

201
00:06:47,664 --> 00:06:49,739
- Did that happen?

202
00:06:49,739 --> 00:06:51,406
- Oh, get technical.

203
00:06:56,095 --> 00:06:59,798
(soft melancholic music)

204
00:06:59,798 --> 00:07:02,158
♫ Sylvia's mother said ♫

205
00:07:02,158 --> 00:07:03,352
- Quiet, Doctor Hook.

206
00:07:03,352 --> 00:07:04,185
- Oh, hmm.

207
00:07:05,159 --> 00:07:07,551
- More sunscreen in aisle seven, sir.

208
00:07:07,551 --> 00:07:08,852
- (chuckles) Oh, I know this movie.

209
00:07:08,852 --> 00:07:11,102
It's "White Men Can't Row."

210
00:07:12,172 --> 00:07:13,951
- Hey, you guys, bad news, the captain

211
00:07:13,951 --> 00:07:15,603
wants to waterski.

212
00:07:15,603 --> 00:07:16,771
My dad told me that one.

213
00:07:16,771 --> 00:07:17,604
- That's pretty funny.

214
00:07:17,604 --> 00:07:18,437
- It's funny.

215
00:07:18,437 --> 00:07:19,428
- Hmm.

216
00:07:19,428 --> 00:07:22,180
- Hey, if you like
Giorgio, you'll love Primo.

217
00:07:22,180 --> 00:07:23,480
♫ Sylvia ♫

218
00:07:23,480 --> 00:07:25,113
- Stop it.

219
00:07:25,113 --> 00:07:26,030
- Oh, yeah.

220
00:07:28,334 --> 00:07:29,251
- I'm long.

221
00:07:30,361 --> 00:07:32,528
(humming)

222
00:07:35,550 --> 00:07:39,845
- If you think he's long, try me, longest.

223
00:07:39,845 --> 00:07:41,845
- Long, longer, longest.

224
00:07:45,918 --> 00:07:48,711
How fast do you figure we're going, Bob?

225
00:07:48,711 --> 00:07:49,544
- Strike a pose.

226
00:07:49,544 --> 00:07:51,309
- Nothing to it.

227
00:07:51,309 --> 00:07:53,861
- I'm tied to the mast.

228
00:07:53,861 --> 00:07:58,028
- Cranky Avalonian slave
ship bingo (chuckles).

229
00:08:01,650 --> 00:08:04,095
- Whoa, Orphil Kidjojapus.

230
00:08:04,095 --> 00:08:07,595
Ooh, I was wondering where that came from.

231
00:08:13,674 --> 00:08:15,595
- Raise the oars, men!

232
00:08:15,595 --> 00:08:18,762
- Raise high the roof beam, carpenter!

233
00:08:20,978 --> 00:08:21,884
- Bravo Bava.

234
00:08:21,884 --> 00:08:26,059
- This movie brought to you
by the letters A, B, and C.

235
00:08:26,059 --> 00:08:29,142
(speaking gibberish)

236
00:08:30,830 --> 00:08:32,032
- Throw over the anchor!

237
00:08:32,032 --> 00:08:34,379
- Why don't you do anything around here?

238
00:08:34,379 --> 00:08:36,520
(chuckling)

239
00:08:36,520 --> 00:08:38,520
Hey, that's the laundry!

240
00:08:40,044 --> 00:08:41,294
Bye, Mr. Hoffa.

241
00:08:42,483 --> 00:08:43,316
- Hey.

242
00:08:44,588 --> 00:08:46,433
(imitating trumpet music)

243
00:08:46,433 --> 00:08:48,451
- Next week, on Genesis 2.

244
00:08:48,451 --> 00:08:49,708
- It's a wagon train.

245
00:08:49,708 --> 00:08:51,734
- [Voiceover] This is the land of Attica.

246
00:08:51,734 --> 00:08:53,817
- Attica, Attica, Attica!

247
00:08:54,758 --> 00:08:57,265
- What new adventures
await Hercules in this,

248
00:08:57,265 --> 00:08:58,366
his native land?

249
00:08:58,366 --> 00:08:59,666
- I get the feeling
you're going to tell us.

250
00:08:59,666 --> 00:09:01,289
- [Voiceover] Many months
ago, he set out alone,

251
00:09:01,289 --> 00:09:03,949
and now he returns with Iole, his bride.

252
00:09:03,949 --> 00:09:05,844
- Hey, stop feeding my bride.

253
00:09:05,844 --> 00:09:08,373
- [Voiceover] Accompanying
Hercules and Iole

254
00:09:08,373 --> 00:09:11,190
to the city of Thebes
will be the young Ulysses,

255
00:09:11,190 --> 00:09:13,162
son of Laërtes.

256
00:09:13,162 --> 00:09:15,330
- Hey, I'm still in here!

257
00:09:15,330 --> 00:09:16,561
- [Voiceover] Now they must bid farewell

258
00:09:16,561 --> 00:09:18,043
to their comrades who have shared

259
00:09:18,043 --> 00:09:20,910
their dangerous adventures
of the last two years.

260
00:09:20,910 --> 00:09:22,882
- Farewell, comrades.

261
00:09:22,882 --> 00:09:24,751
- [Voiceover] Tiphys, dauntless
pilot of the Argonaut.

262
00:09:24,751 --> 00:09:26,013
- And master of knots.

263
00:09:26,013 --> 00:09:28,697
- He thinks he looks like Walter Matthau.

264
00:09:28,697 --> 00:09:31,306
- [Voiceover] Laërtes, the
restless ruler of Ithaca.

265
00:09:31,306 --> 00:09:33,420
- Goes through a lot of skin bronzer.

266
00:09:33,420 --> 00:09:35,134
- [Voiceover] Argo, who
constructed the ship

267
00:09:35,134 --> 00:09:37,770
that served them all so well.

268
00:09:37,770 --> 00:09:40,495
- You bring to Thebes the
most beautiful girl in Jialco.

269
00:09:40,495 --> 00:09:41,328
- Thank you, feces.

270
00:09:41,328 --> 00:09:42,328
- Certainly.

271
00:09:43,669 --> 00:09:46,002
- I'd love to see if anyone
can put him in chains.

272
00:09:46,002 --> 00:09:47,948
- (clears throat) Yeah.

273
00:09:47,948 --> 00:09:49,781
- All ready, Hercules.

274
00:09:51,243 --> 00:09:53,731
- [Laërtes] I ask you this
one favor, because I fear

275
00:09:53,731 --> 00:09:55,602
your judgment is mature.

276
00:09:55,602 --> 00:09:56,761
- Is the horse talking?

277
00:09:56,761 --> 00:09:58,044
- [Laërtes] To be to him like a mother.

278
00:09:58,044 --> 00:10:00,430
Ulysses is only a child
who thinks he's a man

279
00:10:00,430 --> 00:10:02,013
and he'll need you.

280
00:10:04,573 --> 00:10:05,569
- I think he knows.

281
00:10:05,569 --> 00:10:06,402
You'll behave?

282
00:10:06,402 --> 00:10:07,412
- Don't take it seriously.

283
00:10:07,412 --> 00:10:08,545
It's only Father.

284
00:10:08,545 --> 00:10:09,848
- Now, you listen to me.

285
00:10:09,848 --> 00:10:11,315
- Excuse me, but you don't have to worry.

286
00:10:11,315 --> 00:10:12,597
- There, you see?

287
00:10:12,597 --> 00:10:13,626
He has no respect!

288
00:10:13,626 --> 00:10:14,459
- What are these?

289
00:10:14,459 --> 00:10:15,302
- No respect!

290
00:10:15,302 --> 00:10:18,065
- [Laërtes] In time, use one of these.

291
00:10:18,065 --> 00:10:20,956
Carefully tie a message
to the leg of a pigeon

292
00:10:20,956 --> 00:10:22,253
and he'll bring it to me.

293
00:10:22,253 --> 00:10:23,992
- But what are you doing
with my pigeons here?

294
00:10:23,992 --> 00:10:24,825
A present.

295
00:10:24,825 --> 00:10:25,658
They were hers.

296
00:10:25,658 --> 00:10:27,663
Penelope got them at Samos.

297
00:10:27,663 --> 00:10:28,649
- [Laërtes] That's true.

298
00:10:28,649 --> 00:10:30,801
And they'll always fly
back to Ithaca no matter

299
00:10:30,801 --> 00:10:32,140
where you release them.

300
00:10:32,140 --> 00:10:33,333
- What if you release them in Ithaca?

301
00:10:33,333 --> 00:10:34,709
- [Laërtes] And then
discover that these pigeons

302
00:10:34,709 --> 00:10:37,056
can transport the news
quicker than we can.

303
00:10:37,056 --> 00:10:39,806
You will see that the world
will be very different.

304
00:10:39,806 --> 00:10:41,169
- It's only that most
of us feel your pigeons

305
00:10:41,169 --> 00:10:44,424
are better to eat (laughs).

306
00:10:44,424 --> 00:10:45,716
- Farewell, Hercules.

307
00:10:45,716 --> 00:10:46,578
- I don't get it.

308
00:10:46,578 --> 00:10:48,863
- Take care of my son.

309
00:10:48,863 --> 00:10:51,895
- Is it my wife you entrust him to or me?

310
00:10:51,895 --> 00:10:52,728
Here she is.

311
00:10:52,728 --> 00:10:55,245
- Let's bring her out again (whistling).

312
00:10:55,245 --> 00:10:56,972
- Come, help me up.

313
00:10:56,972 --> 00:10:58,287
- Oh, I almost forgot.

314
00:10:58,287 --> 00:10:59,414
- Underwear.

315
00:10:59,414 --> 00:11:00,247
You'll need it.

316
00:11:00,247 --> 00:11:01,812
- This lute, it's from Orpheus.

317
00:11:01,812 --> 00:11:02,645
- Who's that for?

318
00:11:02,645 --> 00:11:04,445
If you expect to play the
lute with those hands,

319
00:11:04,445 --> 00:11:05,805
(Ulysses laughs)

320
00:11:05,805 --> 00:11:07,113
it's for your wife.

321
00:11:07,113 --> 00:11:08,432
- Liar, liar.

322
00:11:08,432 --> 00:11:10,584
Lute's on fire. (chuckles)

323
00:11:10,584 --> 00:11:12,055
- Hmm, looks like a giant egg cutter.

324
00:11:12,055 --> 00:11:14,262
- I will practice.

325
00:11:14,262 --> 00:11:15,226
- Pring.

326
00:11:15,226 --> 00:11:18,303
Well, I was going to
read on the trek, but--

327
00:11:18,303 --> 00:11:19,719
- Please thank him for me.

328
00:11:19,719 --> 00:11:20,719
- Of course.

329
00:11:22,718 --> 00:11:26,385
- Throw this in the
bags marked garage sale.

330
00:11:30,186 --> 00:11:31,019
- Hmm.

331
00:11:31,019 --> 00:11:32,405
- Farewell, Ulysses.

332
00:11:32,405 --> 00:11:35,490
Heed the teachings of Hercules
because one day you will--

333
00:11:35,490 --> 00:11:36,498
- Goodbye, Father.

334
00:11:36,498 --> 00:11:39,811
- I know, so I can get into a good school.

335
00:11:39,811 --> 00:11:40,644
- Hurry, Hercules.

336
00:11:40,644 --> 00:11:42,510
Otherwise we'll all be crying.

337
00:11:42,510 --> 00:11:44,800
(horses neighing)

338
00:11:44,800 --> 00:11:46,849
- Be careful, my son.

339
00:11:46,849 --> 00:11:48,052
- [Ulysses] I will, father!

340
00:11:48,052 --> 00:11:50,842
- Boy, it sure would be
hard to leave all that, huh?

341
00:11:50,842 --> 00:11:52,201
- Have fun storming the castle!

342
00:11:52,201 --> 00:11:53,701
To thy own self be true!

343
00:11:53,701 --> 00:11:56,118
Oh, watch out for that curve!

344
00:11:58,087 --> 00:12:00,254
- Hmm, the high chaparral.

345
00:12:01,939 --> 00:12:03,975
♫ Pom, pom, pom, pom, here comes the king

346
00:12:03,975 --> 00:12:06,296
♫ Here comes the big number one

347
00:12:06,296 --> 00:12:08,851
♫ Here comes ♫

348
00:12:08,851 --> 00:12:10,278
♫ Oh, ho, the Wells Fargo ♫

349
00:12:10,278 --> 00:12:11,111
Come on, everybody!

350
00:12:11,111 --> 00:12:11,944
♫ Oh, ho, the Wells ♫

351
00:12:11,944 --> 00:12:12,777
Oh.

352
00:12:13,794 --> 00:12:15,666
- Tomorrow, we'll see the city of Thebes.

353
00:12:15,666 --> 00:12:17,384
- Oh, big deal, Dad.

354
00:12:17,384 --> 00:12:19,035
- We can tell them all about it.

355
00:12:19,035 --> 00:12:22,040
We want you to know that
we've been listening to you.

356
00:12:22,040 --> 00:12:23,648
We know that the king is Oedipus.

357
00:12:23,648 --> 00:12:24,621
- Who's a fine man.

358
00:12:24,621 --> 00:12:26,994
- And as for Thebes, it's tremendous,

359
00:12:26,994 --> 00:12:28,615
all spacious and rich.

360
00:12:28,615 --> 00:12:30,891
- And the stadium and the
baths and the palaces,

361
00:12:30,891 --> 00:12:33,310
it must be heaven if you
listen to Hercules talk.

362
00:12:33,310 --> 00:12:34,143
(both laugh)

363
00:12:34,143 --> 00:12:35,544
- And the baths and the
malls and the baths and the--

364
00:12:35,544 --> 00:12:36,529
- I don't know what you're talking about.

365
00:12:36,529 --> 00:12:37,362
- I don't get it.

366
00:12:37,362 --> 00:12:39,418
- Now you'll see what a real city is like.

367
00:12:39,418 --> 00:12:40,739
Why, you'll hardly believe your eyes.

368
00:12:40,739 --> 00:12:42,103
- They've got sports bars, you know.

369
00:12:42,103 --> 00:12:43,582
- Manners and courtesy
of the people alone.

370
00:12:43,582 --> 00:12:44,915
- And the baths.

371
00:12:47,030 --> 00:12:50,153
- People bristling with anger.

372
00:12:50,153 --> 00:12:52,655
- Who are those guys?

373
00:12:52,655 --> 00:12:55,236
(loud coughing)

374
00:12:55,236 --> 00:12:57,235
- And their manners are most exquisite.

375
00:12:57,235 --> 00:12:58,529
- They're Argives.

376
00:12:58,529 --> 00:12:59,862
What are they doing in Attica?

377
00:12:59,862 --> 00:13:02,152
- Why worry about it?

378
00:13:02,152 --> 00:13:03,604
- The Argives are fighters.

379
00:13:03,604 --> 00:13:04,966
They live on war.

380
00:13:04,966 --> 00:13:06,432
They thrive on massacres.

381
00:13:06,432 --> 00:13:07,922
- But wasn't their commander a Theban?

382
00:13:07,922 --> 00:13:09,220
Let's go a little faster.

383
00:13:09,220 --> 00:13:10,853
- I will show them.

384
00:13:10,853 --> 00:13:12,241
- Do you want to go faster?

385
00:13:12,241 --> 00:13:13,074
Woo!

386
00:13:14,366 --> 00:13:15,950
- Hercules, that ceremony
you went through,

387
00:13:15,950 --> 00:13:17,661
the bonds of matrimony.

388
00:13:17,661 --> 00:13:18,790
Now you're married.

389
00:13:18,790 --> 00:13:19,925
Drive carefully.

390
00:13:19,925 --> 00:13:21,397
- (chuckles) I'm grateful, Ulysses.

391
00:13:21,397 --> 00:13:22,929
Thanks for the reminder.

392
00:13:22,929 --> 00:13:24,096
- But shut up.

393
00:13:28,082 --> 00:13:28,915
- Oh!

394
00:13:28,915 --> 00:13:29,748
- Who you calling ho?

395
00:13:29,748 --> 00:13:30,581
- So that's the way it is.

396
00:13:30,581 --> 00:13:32,231
Now you're playing games with me.

397
00:13:32,231 --> 00:13:33,559
All right, then.

398
00:13:33,559 --> 00:13:34,392
Have your fun.

399
00:13:34,392 --> 00:13:35,304
I want to rest.

400
00:13:35,304 --> 00:13:36,822
(laughter)

401
00:13:36,822 --> 00:13:38,148
- He ran out of body grease

402
00:13:38,148 --> 00:13:40,065
and he gets all crabby.

403
00:13:40,065 --> 00:13:40,898
- Ha! Ha!

404
00:13:44,450 --> 00:13:45,918
- Hmm. Gee.

405
00:13:45,918 --> 00:13:47,301
Looks like Poppin' Fresh muffins.

406
00:13:47,301 --> 00:13:48,468
- How buttery.

407
00:13:51,655 --> 00:13:53,822
- He's talking to himself.

408
00:13:56,640 --> 00:13:58,107
♫ Nur, nur, nur

409
00:13:58,107 --> 00:13:59,646
♫ Nur, nur, nu-nur ♫

410
00:13:59,646 --> 00:14:03,646
♫ In the jungle, the mighty jungle ♫

411
00:14:03,646 --> 00:14:05,813
(humming)

412
00:14:06,937 --> 00:14:09,698
♫ We all went down to Montreal ♫

413
00:14:09,698 --> 00:14:13,865
♫ Love was in those eyes ♫

414
00:14:16,117 --> 00:14:18,724
♫ Hercules couldn't perform ♫

415
00:14:18,724 --> 00:14:19,905
- Shut up about that.

416
00:14:19,905 --> 00:14:24,627
♫ 'Cause he's using steroids ♫

417
00:14:24,627 --> 00:14:27,377
- She's using the Mel Bay method.

418
00:14:28,877 --> 00:14:32,284
♫ You remain your words to me ♫

419
00:14:32,284 --> 00:14:33,883
- Thank you. Next!

420
00:14:33,883 --> 00:14:37,049
♫ Tell me you are mine

421
00:14:37,049 --> 00:14:40,632
♫ Tell me in the starlight

422
00:14:43,573 --> 00:14:47,740
♫ Last night I was in your arms ♫

423
00:14:49,114 --> 00:14:50,886
- Hey, this is a family show.

424
00:14:50,886 --> 00:14:52,566
♫ My heart still dances ♫

425
00:14:52,566 --> 00:14:54,422
- Herc is trying to sleep back here.

426
00:14:54,422 --> 00:14:57,915
♫ By that evening star

427
00:14:57,915 --> 00:14:59,719
♫ I will walk ♫

428
00:14:59,719 --> 00:15:02,536
♫ Yippi-yi-yo ♫

429
00:15:02,536 --> 00:15:04,904
(imitating dog howling)

430
00:15:04,904 --> 00:15:06,278
♫ Forevermore ♫

431
00:15:06,278 --> 00:15:07,918
- She's going to crack her makeup.

432
00:15:07,918 --> 00:15:11,333
♫ Just you and I

433
00:15:11,333 --> 00:15:14,176
♫ By the evening star ♫

434
00:15:14,176 --> 00:15:16,475
- I think I'll fall on my spear.

435
00:15:16,475 --> 00:15:19,058
(upbeat music)

436
00:15:22,931 --> 00:15:23,848
- Hey! Hey!

437
00:15:25,501 --> 00:15:26,722
Stop a moment, strangers.

438
00:15:26,722 --> 00:15:28,389
This valley is mine.

439
00:15:29,254 --> 00:15:30,579
And no one passes through this valley

440
00:15:30,579 --> 00:15:33,345
unless I say so, and they pay a price.

441
00:15:33,345 --> 00:15:36,475
Yes, this valley is Antaeus'!

442
00:15:36,475 --> 00:15:39,229
And you'll do anything because I say so.

443
00:15:39,229 --> 00:15:40,163
(loud thud)

444
00:15:40,163 --> 00:15:41,045
- Ooh, ow.

445
00:15:41,045 --> 00:15:42,294
All right, go ahead.

446
00:15:42,294 --> 00:15:44,178
- Now, tell me, do you have any gold

447
00:15:44,178 --> 00:15:46,435
hidden in the carriage?

448
00:15:46,435 --> 00:15:48,567
- And the first thing
I'll take are your horses.

449
00:15:48,567 --> 00:15:50,839
Go unharness them for me.

450
00:15:50,839 --> 00:15:52,603
- Hercules! Hercules!

451
00:15:52,603 --> 00:15:54,091
- Oh, I want to sleep.

452
00:15:54,091 --> 00:15:55,539
- Oh, thanks, Hercu-wuss.

453
00:15:55,539 --> 00:15:56,504
- Come on, you get down.

454
00:15:56,504 --> 00:15:57,474
I said I want the horses.

455
00:15:57,474 --> 00:15:59,669
- You take advantage of us
just because you're Antaeus.

456
00:15:59,669 --> 00:16:00,708
- And why not?

457
00:16:00,708 --> 00:16:02,356
Just a boy and a lady.

458
00:16:02,356 --> 00:16:03,361
Come on, now, get down!

459
00:16:03,361 --> 00:16:04,717
- I'll show you what a boy can do.

460
00:16:04,717 --> 00:16:05,717
- I can fly!

461
00:16:06,719 --> 00:16:08,052
- Nice recovery.

462
00:16:10,295 --> 00:16:11,901
- Hercules, he'll kill him!

463
00:16:11,901 --> 00:16:14,407
- I'm so sleepy, I can't
seem to keep awake.

464
00:16:14,407 --> 00:16:16,172
- Oh, that'd be the definition of sleepy.

465
00:16:16,172 --> 00:16:17,618
- Who are you speaking to?

466
00:16:17,618 --> 00:16:18,639
- To my husband.

467
00:16:18,639 --> 00:16:20,407
- And what's he doing?

468
00:16:20,407 --> 00:16:21,511
- He was dozing.

469
00:16:21,511 --> 00:16:22,511
- Dozing, was he?

470
00:16:22,511 --> 00:16:23,941
I'll wake him up.

471
00:16:23,941 --> 00:16:25,085
- I wouldn't do that.

472
00:16:25,085 --> 00:16:26,862
- I know the sleepy husbands,

473
00:16:26,862 --> 00:16:27,978
or is he just frightened?

474
00:16:27,978 --> 00:16:30,026
- He might awaken when he sees you.

475
00:16:30,026 --> 00:16:30,859
- Husband.

476
00:16:31,903 --> 00:16:33,245
- You're my valentine.

477
00:16:33,245 --> 00:16:34,202
- Hey, you, husband.

478
00:16:34,202 --> 00:16:35,035
That's right.

479
00:16:35,035 --> 00:16:36,903
Kiss your lady goodbye and pass on.

480
00:16:36,903 --> 00:16:38,399
I'm adopting the lady.

481
00:16:38,399 --> 00:16:39,416
- Is that right?

482
00:16:39,416 --> 00:16:40,722
- Yes, I'm taking her.

483
00:16:40,722 --> 00:16:42,014
It's my pleasure.

484
00:16:42,014 --> 00:16:43,891
I like her very much, the lady.

485
00:16:43,891 --> 00:16:45,643
- And what does she say about that?

486
00:16:45,643 --> 00:16:50,076
- She'd like a new husband,
like every woman (laughs).

487
00:16:50,076 --> 00:16:52,258
- Ah, awkward moment.

488
00:16:52,258 --> 00:16:53,478
- Hercules.

489
00:16:53,478 --> 00:16:54,860
(loud laughter)

490
00:16:54,860 --> 00:16:55,693
- Hercules!

491
00:16:55,693 --> 00:16:57,999
- He makes Andre the Giant
look like Paul Newman.

492
00:16:57,999 --> 00:17:00,448
- They all turn out to be just like that.

493
00:17:00,448 --> 00:17:02,865
All right, come on and fight.

494
00:17:06,933 --> 00:17:09,168
- What would happen if he really hit him?

495
00:17:09,168 --> 00:17:12,359
- Why is he wearing a bath mat?

496
00:17:12,359 --> 00:17:15,697
- Maybe the next time,
you'll treat me better.

497
00:17:15,697 --> 00:17:17,008
Come on, let's be on our way.

498
00:17:17,008 --> 00:17:19,777
- Well, break out the chest, please.

499
00:17:19,777 --> 00:17:22,026
- He sees the bright side of everything.

500
00:17:22,026 --> 00:17:24,964
(loud laughter)

501
00:17:24,964 --> 00:17:26,532
- You've got a tough skin.

502
00:17:26,532 --> 00:17:29,532
(suspenseful music)

503
00:17:33,011 --> 00:17:36,084
- Lambada, the forbidden dance.

504
00:17:36,084 --> 00:17:39,004
- You know, I had a dream like this once.

505
00:17:39,004 --> 00:17:42,004
- Watch it, I'm wearing my retainer.

506
00:17:42,855 --> 00:17:44,032
- Lower.

507
00:17:44,032 --> 00:17:45,929
I got it, ah.

508
00:17:45,929 --> 00:17:48,929
(suspenseful music)

509
00:17:57,518 --> 00:17:59,843
- Ah, I saw Lucy do this Mr. Mooney once.

510
00:17:59,843 --> 00:18:00,676
- Ooh.

511
00:18:02,704 --> 00:18:04,704
- Oh, I fell on my keys.

512
00:18:08,508 --> 00:18:10,445
- Is this a half nelson or a full nelson?

513
00:18:10,445 --> 00:18:11,747
- Nah, it looks like a Ricky Nelson.

514
00:18:11,747 --> 00:18:13,978
- No, it's just Nelson.

515
00:18:13,978 --> 00:18:14,811
- Ooh.

516
00:18:16,810 --> 00:18:18,746
What scares me is they don't have showers.

517
00:18:18,746 --> 00:18:20,212
- Ooh.

518
00:18:20,212 --> 00:18:21,151
- Okay, you can have me.

519
00:18:21,151 --> 00:18:21,984
I give up.

520
00:18:27,677 --> 00:18:29,451
Rondo Hatton.

521
00:18:29,451 --> 00:18:31,902
- You know, Rondo's good,
'cause you can slam him

522
00:18:31,902 --> 00:18:32,735
down hard.

523
00:18:34,426 --> 00:18:35,259
See?

524
00:18:35,259 --> 00:18:36,317
- Yeah.

525
00:18:36,317 --> 00:18:39,688
- Oh, I see London, I see France.

526
00:18:39,688 --> 00:18:40,521
Huh?

527
00:18:42,364 --> 00:18:45,132
(loud laughter)

528
00:18:45,132 --> 00:18:47,048
- Snicker snag on him, dangle spit.

529
00:18:47,048 --> 00:18:47,881
Come on, Herc!

530
00:18:47,881 --> 00:18:50,055
- Worried about his nipple.

531
00:18:50,055 --> 00:18:51,388
- Any questions?

532
00:18:52,649 --> 00:18:54,234
- Come on, Iole.

533
00:18:54,234 --> 00:18:55,454
(loud laughter)

534
00:18:55,454 --> 00:18:56,550
- Here we go.

535
00:18:56,550 --> 00:18:57,636
- Yeah, I wish he was on our side.

536
00:18:57,636 --> 00:18:58,703
He seems really fun.

537
00:18:58,703 --> 00:19:00,705
(loud laughter)

538
00:19:00,705 --> 00:19:02,019
- He might be a god.

539
00:19:02,019 --> 00:19:03,635
- I don't care if he's Pluto.

540
00:19:03,635 --> 00:19:05,389
I'm going to knock that
silly grin off his face

541
00:19:05,389 --> 00:19:06,806
once and for all.

542
00:19:11,988 --> 00:19:13,793
- I tell you, Hercules,
it must be Antaeus,

543
00:19:13,793 --> 00:19:15,251
son of the earth goddess.

544
00:19:15,251 --> 00:19:17,744
When he touches the ground,
he marshals his forces!

545
00:19:17,744 --> 00:19:18,772
- So that's it.

546
00:19:18,772 --> 00:19:19,980
Then I'll change my way of fighting.

547
00:19:19,980 --> 00:19:22,214
- That's who he said he was.

548
00:19:22,214 --> 00:19:23,514
- Let me down.

549
00:19:23,514 --> 00:19:25,908
Just put me down and you'll see.

550
00:19:25,908 --> 00:19:26,909
- Put me down, put me down!

551
00:19:26,909 --> 00:19:28,716
Mom, Mom, this isn't fun anymore.

552
00:19:28,716 --> 00:19:29,549
Mom!

553
00:19:31,666 --> 00:19:32,874
- I'll spank you.

554
00:19:32,874 --> 00:19:34,017
- Put me down!

555
00:19:34,017 --> 00:19:35,765
Let me down!

556
00:19:35,765 --> 00:19:36,650
(water splashing)

557
00:19:36,650 --> 00:19:39,402
- I've got tubes in my ears!

558
00:19:39,402 --> 00:19:41,053
- There.

559
00:19:41,053 --> 00:19:42,077
- Thanks, friend.

560
00:19:42,077 --> 00:19:44,583
I haven't showered since Zeus was a pup.

561
00:19:44,583 --> 00:19:45,888
- Go on!

562
00:19:45,888 --> 00:19:47,503
But one day you'll have to pass through

563
00:19:47,503 --> 00:19:49,068
my valley again!

564
00:19:49,068 --> 00:19:52,235
- Not after they build the Interstate.

565
00:19:53,503 --> 00:19:56,037
- Virginians, starring James Drury,

566
00:19:56,037 --> 00:19:58,204
brought to you by Nabisco.

567
00:20:05,254 --> 00:20:07,307
- Well, thanks for beating up Antaeus.

568
00:20:07,307 --> 00:20:09,192
I really didn't want to be his wife.

569
00:20:09,192 --> 00:20:10,622
- Just a little wait further.

570
00:20:10,622 --> 00:20:12,482
- There's a gas station.

571
00:20:12,482 --> 00:20:14,189
- I hope we'll be able to rest there.

572
00:20:14,189 --> 00:20:16,023
- I know this forest very well.

573
00:20:16,023 --> 00:20:16,856
Why shouldn't we?

574
00:20:16,856 --> 00:20:18,110
It's quiet here.

575
00:20:18,110 --> 00:20:19,449
They say the gates to the inferno

576
00:20:19,449 --> 00:20:20,996
are hidden among its trees.

577
00:20:20,996 --> 00:20:22,027
- On Broadway.

578
00:20:22,027 --> 00:20:23,562
- But Hercules, look!

579
00:20:23,562 --> 00:20:25,203
- Oh, they're tailgating up ahead.

580
00:20:25,203 --> 00:20:26,764
It must be a Packer game.

581
00:20:26,764 --> 00:20:30,893
- [Hercules] It's the first
time I ever saw anyone here.

582
00:20:30,893 --> 00:20:32,198
- Everybody's making out here.

583
00:20:32,198 --> 00:20:33,031
- Ooh, I'm getting wet.

584
00:20:33,031 --> 00:20:34,114
- Hurry then.

585
00:20:36,859 --> 00:20:38,371
- He's putting a car cover on a horse?

586
00:20:38,371 --> 00:20:39,357
- Stop, what do you want?

587
00:20:39,357 --> 00:20:40,372
- Let her alone.

588
00:20:40,372 --> 00:20:42,233
She's come to keep us company.

589
00:20:42,233 --> 00:20:43,066
What's your name?

590
00:20:43,066 --> 00:20:43,899
- You'll soon find out.

591
00:20:43,899 --> 00:20:44,809
Don't worry.

592
00:20:44,809 --> 00:20:45,642
- Oh, look at that.

593
00:20:45,642 --> 00:20:47,033
She's beginning to fight.

594
00:20:47,033 --> 00:20:48,533
I better tame you.

595
00:20:52,206 --> 00:20:53,623
- Boy, he's bald.

596
00:20:54,937 --> 00:20:56,354
- Not really, no.

597
00:20:58,385 --> 00:21:00,885
- I'm with the big guy, sorry.

598
00:21:01,987 --> 00:21:03,921
- Edward Arnold?

599
00:21:03,921 --> 00:21:04,974
- But wasn't that Hercules?

600
00:21:04,974 --> 00:21:07,541
- He's shorter than his pictures.

601
00:21:07,541 --> 00:21:08,474
(loud laughter)

602
00:21:08,474 --> 00:21:10,701
- Giddy with violence.

603
00:21:10,701 --> 00:21:14,461
- And then we ducked into a little cafe.

604
00:21:14,461 --> 00:21:15,681
- Be quiet.

605
00:21:15,681 --> 00:21:18,257
- [Oedipus] You and
Eteocles, my own children,

606
00:21:18,257 --> 00:21:22,708
plotted to steal my kingdom
and share it between you.

607
00:21:22,708 --> 00:21:24,708
- Mr. Hart, you're late.

608
00:21:25,563 --> 00:21:29,121
- You and your brother have
driven me out of my kingdom.

609
00:21:29,121 --> 00:21:31,435
Only here can I find asylum,

610
00:21:31,435 --> 00:21:33,185
and here I shall die.

611
00:21:34,969 --> 00:21:36,375
- Oedipus.

612
00:21:36,375 --> 00:21:37,208
- Cut, cut.

613
00:21:37,208 --> 00:21:38,625
Hercules, please!

614
00:21:40,540 --> 00:21:42,758
- I know that voice.

615
00:21:42,758 --> 00:21:45,783
It recalls a time in my
life when I was happier.

616
00:21:45,783 --> 00:21:48,268
- Look, it's me, Hercules.

617
00:21:48,268 --> 00:21:50,518
(coughing)

618
00:21:51,906 --> 00:21:54,015
- I came at a bad time, didn't I?

619
00:21:54,015 --> 00:21:57,250
- To me, you are still
the faithful Hercules.

620
00:21:57,250 --> 00:21:58,457
- What are you doing here?

621
00:21:58,457 --> 00:22:00,588
- I'm Ralph Richardson.

622
00:22:00,588 --> 00:22:02,569
- You're Polynices.

623
00:22:02,569 --> 00:22:03,919
- I remember you from the gym.

624
00:22:03,919 --> 00:22:04,827
- You have left Thebes?

625
00:22:04,827 --> 00:22:06,308
- It was not up to me.

626
00:22:06,308 --> 00:22:09,065
My sons thought it better
I renounce the throne,

627
00:22:09,065 --> 00:22:13,445
and so at last, I did, so
that he and his brother

628
00:22:13,445 --> 00:22:15,061
might rule.

629
00:22:15,061 --> 00:22:15,894
- No!

630
00:22:16,988 --> 00:22:18,835
- Give the throne to his brother.

631
00:22:18,835 --> 00:22:22,586
But now Polyneces tells
me that the year is up.

632
00:22:22,586 --> 00:22:23,755
- The god of exposition.

633
00:22:23,755 --> 00:22:25,276
- Look, Father, it's my turn now.

634
00:22:25,276 --> 00:22:27,486
And it's plain to see
just what his brother

635
00:22:27,486 --> 00:22:28,811
wants to do.

636
00:22:28,811 --> 00:22:31,423
♫ It's my turn ♫

637
00:22:31,423 --> 00:22:32,984
- Now, he won't cede to his brother.

638
00:22:32,984 --> 00:22:34,712
He promised to do so.

639
00:22:34,712 --> 00:22:37,878
Now that his year is up, he
has driven his brother away.

640
00:22:37,878 --> 00:22:39,314
- In his new car!

641
00:22:39,314 --> 00:22:42,347
- What do you want of your father?

642
00:22:42,347 --> 00:22:43,811
- Just to pardon us.

643
00:22:43,811 --> 00:22:45,668
- I'm not going to be deceived!

644
00:22:45,668 --> 00:22:48,268
I know just what he wants,
to get to keep the throne

645
00:22:48,268 --> 00:22:50,063
with the help of the Argives.

646
00:22:50,063 --> 00:22:51,922
The throne carries only tragedy.

647
00:22:51,922 --> 00:22:53,875
It can bring no happiness.

648
00:22:53,875 --> 00:22:56,771
Your city will fall
between these two brothers.

649
00:22:56,771 --> 00:22:58,539
- So what I'm hearing here, Polynices,

650
00:22:58,539 --> 00:23:00,349
is you're angry with your father.

651
00:23:00,349 --> 00:23:03,076
- Thebes will be destroyed
and its men will be slain,

652
00:23:03,076 --> 00:23:06,157
and its women, so long as
these two ambitious rulers

653
00:23:06,157 --> 00:23:08,810
get what they want now.

654
00:23:08,810 --> 00:23:10,577
- Now, listen to me, Polynices.

655
00:23:10,577 --> 00:23:12,162
I've known you since you were a child

656
00:23:12,162 --> 00:23:13,542
and I respect your father.

657
00:23:13,542 --> 00:23:15,675
Otherwise, I would exact
justice for Thebes.

658
00:23:15,675 --> 00:23:16,508
- Crossfire.

659
00:23:16,508 --> 00:23:18,096
On the left, Hercules.

660
00:23:18,096 --> 00:23:20,223
- I'll go to your brother
and try to convince him

661
00:23:20,223 --> 00:23:22,354
to respect the pact you made.

662
00:23:22,354 --> 00:23:23,448
- Pact, shmack.

663
00:23:23,448 --> 00:23:25,514
- It's a noble thought
that you have, Hercules,

664
00:23:25,514 --> 00:23:28,125
but my sons will listen to no one.

665
00:23:28,125 --> 00:23:29,621
- But Thebes is my city.

666
00:23:29,621 --> 00:23:31,120
We must spare our people this bloodshed.

667
00:23:31,120 --> 00:23:32,872
- And we built this city on rock and roll.

668
00:23:32,872 --> 00:23:34,757
- Successful in overcoming the madness

669
00:23:34,757 --> 00:23:36,198
of these men, or I'll believe that I--

670
00:23:36,198 --> 00:23:37,031
- Hercules.

671
00:23:37,031 --> 00:23:39,785
- Hercules, am decided by the gods.

672
00:23:39,785 --> 00:23:41,368
- Echo, echo, echo.

673
00:23:42,622 --> 00:23:44,178
- Well, Polynices.

674
00:23:44,178 --> 00:23:45,945
- Well, I can give you a
small part in the chorus,

675
00:23:45,945 --> 00:23:47,195
but that's all.

676
00:23:48,948 --> 00:23:50,547
- If you pass the pencil test.

677
00:23:50,547 --> 00:23:54,047
- If it's better, go with Eteocles, go on.

678
00:23:55,280 --> 00:23:56,410
- I grant you six days.

679
00:23:56,410 --> 00:23:58,399
Let me know if you can
make peace between us.

680
00:23:58,399 --> 00:23:59,998
- At the end of those six
days, we'll march our army

681
00:23:59,998 --> 00:24:01,665
against the Thebans.

682
00:24:03,041 --> 00:24:05,958
(mechanical noise)

683
00:24:11,193 --> 00:24:13,379
♫ And now to Eden

684
00:24:13,379 --> 00:24:16,081
♫ Hey, brother ♫

685
00:24:16,081 --> 00:24:19,083
Haha, Tom, consider the grape.

686
00:24:19,083 --> 00:24:20,785
- Oh, I will.

687
00:24:20,785 --> 00:24:24,868
- So delicate, so firm (laughs).

688
00:24:25,837 --> 00:24:27,331
- You guys, I don't see
why I have to be the one

689
00:24:27,331 --> 00:24:28,297
to peel these grapes.

690
00:24:28,297 --> 00:24:29,904
You know, it's really kind of hard.

691
00:24:29,904 --> 00:24:32,856
- And he calls himself
a hedonist (laughs).

692
00:24:32,856 --> 00:24:35,734
- You know what, I think
it's great that Gypsy

693
00:24:35,734 --> 00:24:38,135
had built this set and
made these costumes for us,

694
00:24:38,135 --> 00:24:39,452
just so she can put on our show.

695
00:24:39,452 --> 00:24:41,870
You guys should do something like that.

696
00:24:41,870 --> 00:24:43,243
- You know, you're right.

697
00:24:43,243 --> 00:24:45,467
Starting right now, I'm going to roll over

698
00:24:45,467 --> 00:24:47,134
and eat more grapes.

699
00:24:48,599 --> 00:24:49,563
- Oh, here she comes.

700
00:24:49,563 --> 00:24:50,878
She's beautiful.

701
00:24:50,878 --> 00:24:52,185
- Hey, looking good, Gypsy.

702
00:24:52,185 --> 00:24:53,018
- Thank you.

703
00:24:53,018 --> 00:24:55,601
And now for a little song in G.

704
00:24:57,668 --> 00:24:59,090
♫ Last night

705
00:24:59,090 --> 00:25:01,257
- Like a beautiful breeze.

706
00:25:02,144 --> 00:25:05,046
♫ Last night

707
00:25:05,046 --> 00:25:08,349
♫ Last night ♫

708
00:25:08,349 --> 00:25:11,501
- So what's she supposed to be, Joel?

709
00:25:11,501 --> 00:25:12,888
- I'm the Hellenistic ideal.

710
00:25:12,888 --> 00:25:13,721
- Oh.

711
00:25:13,721 --> 00:25:15,281
♫ Last night ♫

712
00:25:15,281 --> 00:25:16,202
(loud thud)

713
00:25:16,202 --> 00:25:17,452
- You know, folks, you
just don't hear music

714
00:25:17,452 --> 00:25:18,375
like that anymore.

715
00:25:18,375 --> 00:25:19,354
(loud thud)

716
00:25:19,354 --> 00:25:21,561
- You know, folks, I have
a feeling this is going

717
00:25:21,561 --> 00:25:23,922
to go on like this, so
why don't you run on ahead

718
00:25:23,922 --> 00:25:25,251
into the commercial?

719
00:25:25,251 --> 00:25:27,018
We'll catch up.

720
00:25:27,018 --> 00:25:29,763
♫ Last night, I couldn't
get to sleep at all ♫

721
00:25:29,763 --> 00:25:31,597
- Hey, Joel, am I the only one who notices

722
00:25:31,597 --> 00:25:33,346
I'm not eating a grape?

723
00:25:33,346 --> 00:25:34,971
♫ Last night ♫

724
00:25:34,971 --> 00:25:36,096
Oh, missed.

725
00:25:36,096 --> 00:25:38,679
(upbeat music)

726
00:25:41,978 --> 00:25:43,728
- Hmm, that was good.

727
00:25:45,869 --> 00:25:47,926
- The castle of my father.

728
00:25:47,926 --> 00:25:49,473
- Welcome to my house, Eteocles.

729
00:25:49,473 --> 00:25:51,372
- Two words, Hercules: French doors.

730
00:25:51,372 --> 00:25:52,517
- And you will take the lady with you?

731
00:25:52,517 --> 00:25:53,870
- No, Ulysses will come with me.

732
00:25:53,870 --> 00:25:54,726
- Same thing.

733
00:25:54,726 --> 00:25:55,559
- Ulysses?

734
00:25:55,559 --> 00:25:56,559
Now, who is he?

735
00:25:56,559 --> 00:25:59,343
- Ulysses, son of Laërtes, King of Ithaca.

736
00:25:59,343 --> 00:26:00,499
- A king without soldiers?

737
00:26:00,499 --> 00:26:02,082
I'm not interested.

738
00:26:03,204 --> 00:26:04,037
Take this.

739
00:26:04,037 --> 00:26:04,870
- Put it where the sun don't shine.

740
00:26:04,870 --> 00:26:05,917
- You can tell my brother this.

741
00:26:05,917 --> 00:26:07,372
From now on, what he asks, I will do.

742
00:26:07,372 --> 00:26:08,205
- You've been lifting.

743
00:26:08,205 --> 00:26:09,038
What's your max?

744
00:26:09,038 --> 00:26:12,995
- That's what you're here for, isn't it?

745
00:26:12,995 --> 00:26:14,347
And tomorrow morning, I'll send servants,

746
00:26:14,347 --> 00:26:15,336
goods, and provisions.

747
00:26:15,336 --> 00:26:16,455
- And lawyers, guns, and money.

748
00:26:16,455 --> 00:26:18,768
- If you live alone here in Thebes,

749
00:26:18,768 --> 00:26:19,886
you'll grow impatient.

750
00:26:19,886 --> 00:26:20,865
- Need a roommate?

751
00:26:20,865 --> 00:26:21,766
- Thank you.

752
00:26:21,766 --> 00:26:23,487
- I'll guard Iole until he gets home.

753
00:26:23,487 --> 00:26:25,802
- Ah, then I'm certain
she'll be all right.

754
00:26:25,802 --> 00:26:27,186
- Ouch, grr.

755
00:26:27,186 --> 00:26:31,250
- Creon is the purest and most
intelligent man in Thebes.

756
00:26:31,250 --> 00:26:32,378
- And Creon's nontoxic.

757
00:26:32,378 --> 00:26:34,240
- I'll have Hercules in his way.

758
00:26:34,240 --> 00:26:36,272
I bid you goodbye (laughs).

759
00:26:36,272 --> 00:26:38,900
- Everyone's a comedian.

760
00:26:38,900 --> 00:26:42,644
- Well, I guess it's catch-as-catch-can.

761
00:26:42,644 --> 00:26:46,607
- Next week on Alias Hercules and Ulysses.

762
00:26:46,607 --> 00:26:48,690
- Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow, ow!

763
00:26:51,814 --> 00:26:54,160
- Industry, big and bold.

764
00:26:54,160 --> 00:26:55,834
♫ We are running horses

765
00:26:55,834 --> 00:26:58,253
♫ We are fancy free ♫

766
00:26:58,253 --> 00:27:00,634
- And that's when I won
first prize at the fair.

767
00:27:00,634 --> 00:27:03,258
- Let me out of this cage.

768
00:27:03,258 --> 00:27:05,508
(laughter)

769
00:27:07,003 --> 00:27:08,211
- Well, we must be there.

770
00:27:08,211 --> 00:27:10,461
The music's dying down now.

771
00:27:11,983 --> 00:27:14,749
(laughs) What a fun day.

772
00:27:14,749 --> 00:27:16,552
- Look, cotton.

773
00:27:16,552 --> 00:27:20,719
Meanwhile, Flavius, son of
Magor, is feuding with Crylon.

774
00:27:23,256 --> 00:27:26,329
- I'm pretty sure this
is a Star Trek set here.

775
00:27:26,329 --> 00:27:28,392
- Looks like a Maxfield Parrish painting.

776
00:27:28,392 --> 00:27:30,251
Hmm, kind of.

777
00:27:30,251 --> 00:27:31,643
- Something about this place.

778
00:27:31,643 --> 00:27:33,726
- Reminds me of Appleton.

779
00:27:35,037 --> 00:27:36,620
- Look, I'm hungry.

780
00:27:37,672 --> 00:27:39,667
- Make sure and take good aim.

781
00:27:39,667 --> 00:27:40,500
And remember--

782
00:27:40,500 --> 00:27:41,770
- The distance, the force of the wind,

783
00:27:41,770 --> 00:27:43,010
the speed of the target.

784
00:27:43,010 --> 00:27:44,494
You just decide how you like it

785
00:27:44,494 --> 00:27:45,869
before I get back.

786
00:27:45,869 --> 00:27:47,212
- Well said.

787
00:27:47,212 --> 00:27:48,782
I'll go start the fire up.

788
00:27:48,782 --> 00:27:50,265
And don't come back empty-handed!

789
00:27:50,265 --> 00:27:52,432
- Make sure of the vacuum.

790
00:27:57,258 --> 00:28:01,425
- Well that bird will be
in the next county by now.

791
00:28:06,516 --> 00:28:09,922
- [Voiceover] These are the
waters of forgetfulness.

792
00:28:09,922 --> 00:28:13,687
Those who drink of them will forget all.

793
00:28:13,687 --> 00:28:15,138
(horses neighing)

794
00:28:15,138 --> 00:28:17,790
- He's right, you know.

795
00:28:17,790 --> 00:28:19,013
- What was that?

