1063
00:39:37,844 --> 00:39:40,654
If he's delayed, it's something logical.

1064
00:39:40,654 --> 00:39:43,009
But I feel so anxious when I don't hear.

1065
00:39:43,009 --> 00:39:45,058
- We should have at least
gotten a pigeon by now.

1066
00:39:45,058 --> 00:39:46,593
- I'll stay only until tomorrow morning,

1067
00:39:46,593 --> 00:39:49,361
and then I'll go to see
if I can locate him.

1068
00:39:49,361 --> 00:39:53,002
- I'll call the finder of lost loves.

1069
00:39:53,002 --> 00:39:56,419
- All of a sudden, it's paint your wagon.

1070
00:39:59,600 --> 00:40:03,387
♫ Peace on earth was all he said

1071
00:40:03,387 --> 00:40:05,233
♫ Du, du, dudududu ♫

1072
00:40:05,233 --> 00:40:08,233
- Hey, I can see my house from here!

1073
00:40:09,228 --> 00:40:10,728
- Bird lives, woo!

1074
00:40:12,547 --> 00:40:14,913
- I thought I say Ulysses.

1075
00:40:14,913 --> 00:40:15,746
I did it!

1076
00:40:15,746 --> 00:40:17,246
I did see Ulysses.

1077
00:40:18,374 --> 00:40:20,124
- You guys wait here.

1078
00:40:27,080 --> 00:40:30,460
- Hmm, I was just doing
the dishes, hmm-hmm.

1079
00:40:30,460 --> 00:40:32,857
- Come on, you're going to work, now, now!

1080
00:40:32,857 --> 00:40:36,190
- I've got to finish these dishes first.

1081
00:40:39,815 --> 00:40:43,293
(suspenseful music)

1082
00:40:43,293 --> 00:40:48,158
- My boy, I have discovered
something very important.

1083
00:40:48,158 --> 00:40:49,070
- This really bugs me.

1084
00:40:49,070 --> 00:40:52,333
- Up to now, I've been
making one big mistake.

1085
00:40:52,333 --> 00:40:54,207
- Hey, is he turtlewaxing him?

1086
00:40:54,207 --> 00:40:56,535
- And stay awake at night.

1087
00:40:56,535 --> 00:40:59,711
Otherwise, you'll lose the
best part of your life.

1088
00:40:59,711 --> 00:41:03,878
- I can see you've been really
thinking deep here, sir.

1089
00:41:07,165 --> 00:41:08,325
- Hey, it's tea.

1090
00:41:08,325 --> 00:41:11,270
You know, that's hard to find around here.

1091
00:41:11,270 --> 00:41:14,095
(soft music)

1092
00:41:14,095 --> 00:41:15,512
- Is it prepared?

1093
00:41:18,970 --> 00:41:19,803
- Hmm.

1094
00:41:20,961 --> 00:41:22,044
Dinner, Herc.

1095
00:41:22,925 --> 00:41:23,758
- Ah, yes.

1096
00:41:23,758 --> 00:41:26,091
The night was made for love.

1097
00:41:27,815 --> 00:41:30,732
The sun out there dulls the senses.

1098
00:41:32,155 --> 00:41:33,738
Enough. I'm hungry.

1099
00:41:35,894 --> 00:41:37,429
- Oh, I think he just
insulted the waitress.

1100
00:41:37,429 --> 00:41:38,833
- Haha, what a life.

1101
00:41:38,833 --> 00:41:40,615
(women giggling)

1102
00:41:40,615 --> 00:41:42,918
You wake up in the morning
without a care in the world

1103
00:41:42,918 --> 00:41:44,102
and nothing to do.

1104
00:41:44,102 --> 00:41:47,615
- Just like collecting
unemployment checks.

1105
00:41:47,615 --> 00:41:48,825
(loud crash)

1106
00:41:48,825 --> 00:41:51,232
- The heck you doing there?

1107
00:41:51,232 --> 00:41:52,315
- Ah, clumsy.

1108
00:41:53,368 --> 00:41:56,473
It looks like you did it on purpose.

1109
00:41:56,473 --> 00:41:57,473
- Shh!

1110
00:41:57,473 --> 00:41:59,306
- Let's play charades.

1111
00:42:00,427 --> 00:42:03,042
- Okay, I'll go along.

1112
00:42:03,042 --> 00:42:05,650
- Look to the left, look to the right,

1113
00:42:05,650 --> 00:42:08,733
stand, sit down, fight, fight, fight!

1114
00:42:10,572 --> 00:42:12,680
- This is the fountain of dorkiness.

1115
00:42:12,680 --> 00:42:14,930
- Got any ketchup for this?

1116
00:42:16,901 --> 00:42:18,456
- Don't tell.

1117
00:42:18,456 --> 00:42:20,312
- You are Hercules.

1118
00:42:20,312 --> 00:42:21,145
- Pff!

1119
00:42:24,267 --> 00:42:25,100
- What did you say?

1120
00:42:25,100 --> 00:42:26,028
- I forgot already.

1121
00:42:26,028 --> 00:42:27,246
- Hercules.

1122
00:42:27,246 --> 00:42:28,163
- Hercules?

1123
00:42:29,783 --> 00:42:31,825
What about Hercules?

1124
00:42:31,825 --> 00:42:33,242
- Iole.

1125
00:42:33,242 --> 00:42:37,135
- Go away, I don't understand a thing.

1126
00:42:37,135 --> 00:42:39,032
- Iole, your marriage,
Eteocles, Polynices,

1127
00:42:39,032 --> 00:42:40,774
the message, the perilous
war against Thebes.

1128
00:42:40,774 --> 00:42:43,698
- Things you'd say to Socrates.

1129
00:42:43,698 --> 00:42:46,531
(quick footsteps)

1130
00:42:49,479 --> 00:42:50,443
- Bend it.

1131
00:42:50,443 --> 00:42:51,987
If you can't, you'll convince me.

1132
00:42:51,987 --> 00:42:54,889
- If you can, you're Uri Geller.

1133
00:42:54,889 --> 00:42:58,873
- You're lucky I'm in
a good mood, Ulysses.

1134
00:42:58,873 --> 00:43:01,540
(loud grunting)

1135
00:43:06,791 --> 00:43:08,677
- Rats, I can't bend it.

1136
00:43:08,677 --> 00:43:12,510
Guess I have to stay
here with all the nymphs.

1137
00:43:18,941 --> 00:43:20,371
- Hit the road, Pedro.

1138
00:43:20,371 --> 00:43:21,454
Oh, hi, Herc.

1139
00:43:23,401 --> 00:43:25,977
♫ Wawawawawawa

1140
00:43:25,977 --> 00:43:27,848
♫ Rarararara ♫

1141
00:43:27,848 --> 00:43:29,193
- Good morning.

1142
00:43:29,193 --> 00:43:31,610
(soft music)

1143
00:43:33,278 --> 00:43:35,007
- Did you sleep well last night?

1144
00:43:35,007 --> 00:43:36,111
- Wonderfully.

1145
00:43:36,111 --> 00:43:37,444
I dreamt of you.

1146
00:43:39,888 --> 00:43:41,382
- And I'm flattered.

1147
00:43:41,382 --> 00:43:44,275
- And flattery will get you everywhere.

1148
00:43:44,275 --> 00:43:48,515
- Ah, old ball and chain (chuckles).

1149
00:43:48,515 --> 00:43:49,929
- So, what's on the slate today,

1150
00:43:49,929 --> 00:43:52,191
eating and loving, huh?

1151
00:43:52,191 --> 00:43:54,917
- Somehow I recall that
you had a different face.

1152
00:43:54,917 --> 00:43:56,535
- Yeah, it was fillers stillers.

1153
00:43:56,535 --> 00:43:57,368
I had to return it.

1154
00:43:57,368 --> 00:43:58,201
- Prettier?

1155
00:43:58,201 --> 00:43:59,415
- No, just different.

1156
00:43:59,415 --> 00:44:02,081
Blond hair, sweet smile.

1157
00:44:02,081 --> 00:44:03,437
- Hair growing out of your wart.

1158
00:44:03,437 --> 00:44:07,270
- So you've begun to
betray me in your dreams.

1159
00:44:08,391 --> 00:44:09,428
- Aren't you afraid that somehow

1160
00:44:09,428 --> 00:44:11,013
we'd displease the fates

1161
00:44:11,013 --> 00:44:12,854
and they'll take their revenge on us?

1162
00:44:12,854 --> 00:44:14,733
- I try not to think about it.

1163
00:44:14,733 --> 00:44:15,650
So, anyway.

1164
00:44:18,737 --> 00:44:21,294
- I don't want to talk about sad things

1165
00:44:21,294 --> 00:44:22,428
when I'm so happy.

1166
00:44:22,428 --> 00:44:23,345
I love you.

1167
00:44:25,277 --> 00:44:27,860
For me, that's all that counts.

1168
00:44:29,041 --> 00:44:31,624
(upbeat music)

1169
00:44:35,852 --> 00:44:37,806
- [Magic Voice] This is
the water of forgetfulness.

1170
00:44:37,806 --> 00:44:39,822
Those who drink of it will forget all.

1171
00:44:39,822 --> 00:44:41,138
- Huh, say, who manufactures

1172
00:44:41,138 --> 00:44:42,569
the water of forgetfulness anyway?

1173
00:44:42,569 --> 00:44:45,820
- Oh, it says here on the
bottle, Mendota Springs,

1174
00:44:45,820 --> 00:44:50,255
makers of the water of
forgetfulness, since, oh,

1175
00:44:50,255 --> 00:44:51,829
let me think.

1176
00:44:51,829 --> 00:44:54,628
Oh, it's on the tip of my tongue.

1177
00:44:54,628 --> 00:44:55,593
When was it?

1178
00:44:55,593 --> 00:44:58,374
- [Magic Voice] This is the
carrot shake of pretentiousness.

1179
00:44:58,374 --> 00:44:59,273
- Ooh, let me try that.

1180
00:44:59,273 --> 00:45:00,190
- [Magic Voice] Those who drink of it

1181
00:45:00,190 --> 00:45:02,157
will join theater companies.

1182
00:45:02,157 --> 00:45:04,242
- Yeah, you know, I'm doing
an anti-Columbus thing

1183
00:45:04,242 --> 00:45:06,352
down at the heart of the
Meat Puppet Beast Theater.

1184
00:45:06,352 --> 00:45:08,460
It's a real opportunity for me to stretch.

1185
00:45:08,460 --> 00:45:09,637
- Hey, Joel, that cup looks like

1186
00:45:09,637 --> 00:45:10,527
it's from Dairy Queen.

1187
00:45:10,527 --> 00:45:11,360
Can I have some?

1188
00:45:11,360 --> 00:45:12,193
- Hmm.

1189
00:45:12,193 --> 00:45:14,313
- [Magic Voice] This is
the blizzard of loneliness.

1190
00:45:14,313 --> 00:45:15,775
Those who drink of it
will sit on the beach

1191
00:45:15,775 --> 00:45:17,793
wearing long pants and black socks

1192
00:45:17,793 --> 00:45:19,326
and look for change in the sand

1193
00:45:19,326 --> 00:45:20,818
with a metal detector.

1194
00:45:20,818 --> 00:45:22,366
- I found a quarter!

1195
00:45:22,366 --> 00:45:23,468
- Hey, who wants gum?

1196
00:45:23,468 --> 00:45:24,346
- I do, I do!

1197
00:45:24,346 --> 00:45:25,179
- Here.

1198
00:45:25,179 --> 00:45:27,598
- [Magic Voice] You're eating
the fruit stripe of stability.

1199
00:45:27,598 --> 00:45:30,032
Those who chew it will
get a civil service job

1200
00:45:30,032 --> 00:45:31,521
with good benefits.

1201
00:45:31,521 --> 00:45:33,405
- Yup, thanks to the fruit
stripe gum of stability,

1202
00:45:33,405 --> 00:45:35,227
I've got a good dental plan now.

1203
00:45:35,227 --> 00:45:36,227
Ironic, huh?

1204
00:45:37,075 --> 00:45:38,258
- [Magic Voice] You are
eating the green bean

1205
00:45:38,258 --> 00:45:40,574
and french onion casserole of happiness.

1206
00:45:40,574 --> 00:45:42,498
Those who eat of it will find the serenity

1207
00:45:42,498 --> 00:45:44,766
that only a hot dish can bring.

1208
00:45:44,766 --> 00:45:47,900
- Oh, you know, I really,
really love this stuff.

1209
00:45:47,900 --> 00:45:51,022
It's so nutritious and
it's so good for you.

1210
00:45:51,022 --> 00:45:52,639
And I love my location.

1211
00:45:52,639 --> 00:45:55,700
It's so conveniently
located, what with the chains

1212
00:45:55,700 --> 00:45:58,852
and dinner theater and
the new high school,

1213
00:45:58,852 --> 00:46:02,989
and oh the elks lodge puts
on a wonderful fish fry

1214
00:46:02,989 --> 00:46:04,511
every weekend.

1215
00:46:04,511 --> 00:46:07,151
And we're right next
to the chain of lakes.

1216
00:46:07,151 --> 00:46:08,816
And we've got movie signs.

1217
00:46:08,816 --> 00:46:11,755
And they do the big
Chautauqua show every summer.

1218
00:46:11,755 --> 00:46:13,187
And they've got movie signs.

1219
00:46:13,187 --> 00:46:14,437
Movie sign? Oh!

1220
00:46:16,304 --> 00:46:19,221
(mechanical noise)

1221
00:46:25,761 --> 00:46:27,053
- Hot dish is filling, isn't it?

1222
00:46:27,053 --> 00:46:28,871
- Oh, yeah, it's so good.

1223
00:46:28,871 --> 00:46:30,939
- Peter, Paul, and Mary.

1224
00:46:30,939 --> 00:46:32,388
- And where did they find the princess?

1225
00:46:32,388 --> 00:46:33,292
- The Personals.

1226
00:46:33,292 --> 00:46:35,039
- Just planning to run away

1227
00:46:35,039 --> 00:46:36,779
because she couldn't stand Thebes

1228
00:46:36,779 --> 00:46:38,532
and she wanted to rejoin her husband.

1229
00:46:38,532 --> 00:46:39,865
- Walk this way.

1230
00:46:41,308 --> 00:46:42,141
- Stop.

1231
00:46:43,429 --> 00:46:46,117
- Did you hear from Hercules?

1232
00:46:46,117 --> 00:46:48,056
- Well, just a message on my machine.

1233
00:46:48,056 --> 00:46:49,050
- Not a word since he's away.

1234
00:46:49,050 --> 00:46:52,218
And I'll I've done was wait here alone.

1235
00:46:52,218 --> 00:46:55,237
And if I did run away, it was only...

1236
00:46:55,237 --> 00:46:56,989
I beg you to let me go to Hercules.

1237
00:46:56,989 --> 00:46:58,339
- And let me smoke in my room.

1238
00:46:58,339 --> 00:46:59,672
- That would be splendid for you two, huh?

1239
00:46:59,672 --> 00:47:02,808
Reunited under the tender
care of my brother Polynices.

1240
00:47:02,808 --> 00:47:04,796
- I don't see what you mean, sir.

1241
00:47:04,796 --> 00:47:06,623
- Well, it's not her fault, Eteocles.

1242
00:47:06,623 --> 00:47:08,144
And why blame Hercules?

1243
00:47:08,144 --> 00:47:11,096
Don't you see, if you let
them go to each other, then--

1244
00:47:11,096 --> 00:47:11,929
- Stop yelling!

1245
00:47:11,929 --> 00:47:13,450
Why is everybody yelling?

1246
00:47:13,450 --> 00:47:14,700
- You talk to me as if
I'm prepared to take leave

1247
00:47:14,700 --> 00:47:16,520
of my senses.

1248
00:47:16,520 --> 00:47:17,501
Take the woman away.

1249
00:47:17,501 --> 00:47:19,336
- Well, they're posing
for the Primo beer can.

1250
00:47:19,336 --> 00:47:20,516
- Cool.

1251
00:47:20,516 --> 00:47:22,599
- That's unjust, inhuman.

1252
00:47:25,394 --> 00:47:27,659
- I shall now arrest any
and all Theban suspected

1253
00:47:27,659 --> 00:47:29,782
of plotting with Polynices!

1254
00:47:29,782 --> 00:47:30,745
Arrest them all!

1255
00:47:30,745 --> 00:47:31,578
- They left, sir.

1256
00:47:31,578 --> 00:47:35,036
- With their goods and
families and servants!

1257
00:47:35,036 --> 00:47:36,819
- Can't we just arrest everyone in red?

1258
00:47:36,819 --> 00:47:39,050
- You who all pretend
that you want justice.

1259
00:47:39,050 --> 00:47:42,491
That nobody Hercules and
my friends here in court.

1260
00:47:42,491 --> 00:47:43,324
- Cut!

1261
00:47:44,507 --> 00:47:46,787
- Creon will be my example.

1262
00:47:46,787 --> 00:47:47,752
- What about El Marco?

1263
00:47:47,752 --> 00:47:48,835
- Arrest him.

1264
00:47:55,006 --> 00:47:56,839
- Made you look, haha.

1265
00:48:02,197 --> 00:48:04,097
- And now, a journey
through the lymph nodes.

1266
00:48:04,097 --> 00:48:05,281
- You mean, nymph lodes.

1267
00:48:05,281 --> 00:48:06,114
- Ooh.

1268
00:48:07,966 --> 00:48:10,914
- Ah, working out a new filing system.

1269
00:48:10,914 --> 00:48:11,747
All right.

1270
00:48:14,727 --> 00:48:18,162
(imitates loud snoring)

1271
00:48:18,162 --> 00:48:20,114
- Wake up, it's time to go to work.

1272
00:48:20,114 --> 00:48:21,697
Get out of bed now.

1273
00:48:23,170 --> 00:48:27,138
- I can't hear you, I'm sleeping and deaf.

1274
00:48:27,138 --> 00:48:28,217
- Get up now, it's late.

1275
00:48:28,217 --> 00:48:30,051
Your master's waiting for his massage.

1276
00:48:30,051 --> 00:48:32,051
- At two in the morning?

1277
00:48:36,154 --> 00:48:38,443
- Massage this, you cretin.

1278
00:48:38,443 --> 00:48:39,693
I mean, cretin.

1279
00:48:40,610 --> 00:48:43,453
(playful music)

1280
00:48:43,453 --> 00:48:45,793
- Creon will be played by the bassoon.

1281
00:48:45,793 --> 00:48:49,341
♫ Dududududu ♫

1282
00:48:49,341 --> 00:48:50,966
- What the heck is going on here?

1283
00:48:50,966 --> 00:48:55,133
♫ Dun dun dun dun dulululu dun dun ♫

1284
00:48:56,656 --> 00:48:57,827
- Ah, yeah, like no one's going to notice

1285
00:48:57,827 --> 00:48:59,804
the string on the lock.

1286
00:48:59,804 --> 00:49:01,833
- Here's our Hercules power wrist band.

1287
00:49:01,833 --> 00:49:02,666
- Nice.

1288
00:49:03,889 --> 00:49:06,889
(suspenseful music)

1289
00:49:12,538 --> 00:49:13,629
- Shh!

1290
00:49:13,629 --> 00:49:14,796
- Coming, Mom!

1291
00:49:15,931 --> 00:49:18,069
- Mm, big old jelly doughnut.

1292
00:49:18,069 --> 00:49:19,819
Oh, boy, I love this.

1293
00:49:21,225 --> 00:49:22,058
Hmm. Ah.

1294
00:49:23,295 --> 00:49:26,295
(suspenseful music)

1295
00:49:27,912 --> 00:49:29,093
(loud crash)

1296
00:49:29,093 --> 00:49:33,975
- You are nuttier than an
outhouse rat, you know that?

1297
00:49:33,975 --> 00:49:36,061
- That's the second time
you knocked over my goblet.

1298
00:49:36,061 --> 00:49:37,081
- How would you remember that?

1299
00:49:37,081 --> 00:49:40,129
- I do it for you, Hercules.

1300
00:49:40,129 --> 00:49:42,336
- Why is it you keep
on calling me Hercules?

1301
00:49:42,336 --> 00:49:44,586
- You know my name is Todd.

1302
00:49:46,606 --> 00:49:50,121
- Hmm, really, tore through
those bare claws, didn't you?

1303
00:49:50,121 --> 00:49:51,589
- I've heard that name before.

1304
00:49:51,589 --> 00:49:52,955
- You'll see, soon you'll remember.

1305
00:49:52,955 --> 00:49:54,516
- Just look at your chariot license.

1306
00:49:54,516 --> 00:49:55,349
- Remember what?

1307
00:49:55,349 --> 00:49:56,349
- It's too complicated
to explain to you now.

1308
00:49:56,349 --> 00:49:58,344
I beg you to avoid drinking that water.

1309
00:49:58,344 --> 00:49:59,420
Then you'll recover your memory

1310
00:49:59,420 --> 00:50:01,214
and soon we'll be able to escape.

1311
00:50:01,214 --> 00:50:02,613
Escape from this, why?

1312
00:50:02,613 --> 00:50:03,586
- Go away?

1313
00:50:03,586 --> 00:50:06,000
Isn't this your native land?

1314
00:50:06,000 --> 00:50:08,723
- You and I have been comrades.

1315
00:50:08,723 --> 00:50:11,197
We were captured and brought here.

1316
00:50:11,197 --> 00:50:13,390
I tell you that we must get out of here.

1317
00:50:13,390 --> 00:50:15,084
What I saw was so terrible!

1318
00:50:15,084 --> 00:50:16,482
- Curly Sue?

1319
00:50:16,482 --> 00:50:19,220
- You see, during the
day, they don't bother me.

1320
00:50:19,220 --> 00:50:22,209
At night, I'm put into a
cell and locked inside.

1321
00:50:22,209 --> 00:50:24,174
Yesterday, I was looking
for a means to get out.

1322
00:50:24,174 --> 00:50:25,292
- That's dippity do!

1323
00:50:25,292 --> 00:50:27,325
- I saw a path leading to a cave.

1324
00:50:27,325 --> 00:50:29,078
- Let me demonstrate.

1325
00:50:29,078 --> 00:50:33,245
♫ Into the woods, into the woods ♫

1326
00:50:34,098 --> 00:50:35,452
Dad?

1327
00:50:35,452 --> 00:50:38,966
(suspenseful music)

1328
00:50:38,966 --> 00:50:40,633
It's not that scary.

1329
00:50:41,603 --> 00:50:42,770
- Well, maybe.

1330
00:50:43,619 --> 00:50:46,619
(suspenseful music)

1331
00:50:48,107 --> 00:50:50,409
- Oh, it's Kim Cattrall.

1332
00:50:50,409 --> 00:50:51,242
- It's scary.

1333
00:50:51,242 --> 00:50:53,077
- Nice skort.

1334
00:50:53,077 --> 00:50:56,719
- Sir, please don't touch
the exhibit, please.

1335
00:50:56,719 --> 00:50:57,552
- Yeah!

1336
00:50:59,764 --> 00:51:03,097
- And then I came to another passage and

1337
00:51:04,684 --> 00:51:06,425
it's Madame Tussauds.

1338
00:51:06,425 --> 00:51:07,258
- Oh!

1339
00:51:11,455 --> 00:51:12,711
Now just about that time...

1340
00:51:12,711 --> 00:51:13,661
Are you listening to me?

1341
00:51:13,661 --> 00:51:14,494
Good.

1342
00:51:14,494 --> 00:51:17,448
Wait, this is a disco inferno!

1343
00:51:17,448 --> 00:51:18,281
- Hmm.

1344
00:51:19,518 --> 00:51:21,419
- Suddenly, people showed up.

1345
00:51:21,419 --> 00:51:24,839
You meet them wherever you're going.

1346
00:51:24,839 --> 00:51:26,371
(suspenseful music)

1347
00:51:26,371 --> 00:51:28,918
- Oh, hi, Rey, hi, Rel.

1348
00:51:28,918 --> 00:51:32,972
- Looks like a cheap Temple of Doom set.

1349
00:51:32,972 --> 00:51:33,925
- Ooh!

1350
00:51:33,925 --> 00:51:35,912
- Oh, cool, it's like a Thing maker.

1351
00:51:35,912 --> 00:51:38,723
- She's got Batman underwear on!

1352
00:51:38,723 --> 00:51:39,556
- Cool!

1353
00:51:39,556 --> 00:51:41,296
- You Egyptians are truly so clever

1354
00:51:41,296 --> 00:51:42,830
that almost certainly you'll find a way

1355
00:51:42,830 --> 00:51:44,678
of even preserving life.

1356
00:51:44,678 --> 00:51:45,784
- Life is different.

1357
00:51:45,784 --> 00:51:47,985
We can't create the soul of man.

1358
00:51:47,985 --> 00:51:51,104
- Still, it must be exciting, your work.

1359
00:51:51,104 --> 00:51:52,721
- Look, I just told you it's different.

1360
00:51:52,721 --> 00:51:55,471
- Just the man, the way he looks,

1361
00:51:56,506 --> 00:51:58,457
the way he stands.

1362
00:51:58,457 --> 00:52:00,840
- When can we expect to
get to work on Hercules?

1363
00:52:00,840 --> 00:52:02,153
- Well, let's see, I've
got an eight o'clock

1364
00:52:02,153 --> 00:52:04,320
and a nine-thirty, and oh.

1365
00:52:06,288 --> 00:52:08,025
- Gotta go. Bye.

1366
00:52:08,025 --> 00:52:08,858
Come on, girls.

1367
00:52:08,858 --> 00:52:10,093
- Wait, wait, come back!

1368
00:52:10,093 --> 00:52:12,426
You forgot your free casket!

1369
00:52:15,348 --> 00:52:17,403
- Was this a Remington Steel episode?

1370
00:52:17,403 --> 00:52:18,236
- I think so.

1371
00:52:18,236 --> 00:52:19,525
- I tremble with fear
at what she plans to do

1372
00:52:19,525 --> 00:52:21,841
with us, Hercules.

1373
00:52:21,841 --> 00:52:23,219
- Why should I believe you?

1374
00:52:23,219 --> 00:52:24,286
- I expected that.

1375
00:52:24,286 --> 00:52:25,584
- What's that supposed to mean?

1376
00:52:25,584 --> 00:52:28,490
- I'm going to ask the queen
to see if you're lying.

1377
00:52:28,490 --> 00:52:29,944
- Omphale will be sure to deny it.

1378
00:52:29,944 --> 00:52:32,067
She'll kill me, and then
what will happen to you?

1379
00:52:32,067 --> 00:52:33,115
I prefer to be killed by you

1380
00:52:33,115 --> 00:52:34,381
rather than that way.

1381
00:52:34,381 --> 00:52:36,371
- Why, thank you.

1382
00:52:36,371 --> 00:52:37,778
- I promise you, I won't speak anymore

1383
00:52:37,778 --> 00:52:39,945
about Hercules or Omphale.

1384
00:52:41,562 --> 00:52:42,395
- Ah.

1385
00:52:47,183 --> 00:52:49,642
Cripes, I am the Herc.

1386
00:52:49,642 --> 00:52:51,537
(loud clanging)

1387
00:52:51,537 --> 00:52:54,120
- Just set that anywhere, Herc.

1388
00:53:00,330 --> 00:53:01,830
- Hi, who are you?

1389
00:53:04,611 --> 00:53:06,234
- You jerk, you bent my lamp.

1390
00:53:06,234 --> 00:53:07,401
- No, you did!

1391
00:53:08,418 --> 00:53:09,251
- Did not.

1392
00:53:14,195 --> 00:53:15,028
There.

1393
00:53:15,028 --> 00:53:15,861
- It's still bent.

1394
00:53:15,861 --> 00:53:18,611
They're going to be able to tell.

1395
00:53:19,448 --> 00:53:21,280
(loud clanging)

1396
00:53:21,280 --> 00:53:22,113
He's back.

1397
00:53:24,116 --> 00:53:25,768
- Wahahahaha!

1398
00:53:25,768 --> 00:53:27,091
- I'm coo coo for cocoa puffs,

1399
00:53:27,091 --> 00:53:28,436
coo coo for cocoa puffs!

1400
00:53:28,436 --> 00:53:30,207
- A little embarrassing.

1401
00:53:30,207 --> 00:53:32,874
(loud giggling)

1402
00:53:37,157 --> 00:53:39,606
(loud laughter)

1403
00:53:39,606 --> 00:53:42,535
- I can't believe I liked him.

1404
00:53:42,535 --> 00:53:43,967
- Jeez, turning into Harpo.

1405
00:53:43,967 --> 00:53:45,128
- Yeah.

1406
00:53:45,128 --> 00:53:47,681
(women giggling)

1407
00:53:47,681 --> 00:53:52,216
- When Kennedys rule Greece (chuckles).

1408
00:53:52,216 --> 00:53:55,192
- Uh-oh, Heather's dad is here, guys.

1409
00:53:55,192 --> 00:53:58,609
(imitates trumpet music)

1410
00:54:01,726 --> 00:54:03,363
- So, now, what we've done with Hercules

1411
00:54:03,363 --> 00:54:05,342
is minimize his large
forehead with this flower ring

1412
00:54:05,342 --> 00:54:08,866
and accentuate his massive chest.

1413
00:54:08,866 --> 00:54:10,569
- Go away now.

1414
00:54:10,569 --> 00:54:11,922
I just said leave me!

1415
00:54:11,922 --> 00:54:14,505
- Oh, my, what happened to him?

1416
00:54:16,422 --> 00:54:17,996
- I never get tired of that.

1417
00:54:17,996 --> 00:54:20,741
- No one ever dared give
an order in my presence.

1418
00:54:20,741 --> 00:54:22,304
- No one else is the Herc-meister.

1419
00:54:22,304 --> 00:54:25,054
- Well, it's only the first time.

1420
00:54:26,573 --> 00:54:29,643
- Hey, it's nine-thirty, honey.

1421
00:54:29,643 --> 00:54:30,784
- So what are they doing?

1422
00:54:30,784 --> 00:54:31,617
- Oh, wow!

1423
00:54:32,813 --> 00:54:35,195
- Mm, he's Herculicious!

1424
00:54:35,195 --> 00:54:36,213
- What are they up to, Joel?

1425
00:54:36,213 --> 00:54:38,963
(romantic music)

1426
00:54:40,880 --> 00:54:43,353
- You have a strange power over me.

1427
00:54:43,353 --> 00:54:44,275
- Power of attorney.

1428
00:54:44,275 --> 00:54:46,330
- Whether it's love or not, I don't know.

1429
00:54:46,330 --> 00:54:47,774
- I don't think it is.

1430
00:54:47,774 --> 00:54:50,221
- And yet all I want
is just to be with you.

1431
00:54:50,221 --> 00:54:51,274
- That's the way I like it.

1432
00:54:51,274 --> 00:54:52,691
- Uh-huh. Uh-huh.

1433
00:54:53,718 --> 00:54:55,790
- Bet he says that to all the queens.

1434
00:54:55,790 --> 00:54:57,707
- Oh, more gushy stuff.

1435
00:54:59,163 --> 00:55:00,184
Hmm?

1436
00:55:00,184 --> 00:55:01,446
(trumpet blasting)

1437
00:55:01,446 --> 00:55:02,748
Ricola?

1438
00:55:02,748 --> 00:55:05,192
(coughing)

1439
00:55:05,192 --> 00:55:06,025
- What was that?

1440
00:55:06,025 --> 00:55:06,858
- It's my pager.

1441
00:55:06,858 --> 00:55:07,691
- Great queen.

1442
00:55:07,691 --> 00:55:08,860
- Thanks!

1443
00:55:08,860 --> 00:55:11,193
- Arrived with a small crew.

1444
00:55:13,686 --> 00:55:15,084
They want to stay here several days.

1445
00:55:15,084 --> 00:55:17,071
They are waiting to
present their respects.

1446
00:55:17,071 --> 00:55:18,072
- Tell them to go away!

1447
00:55:18,072 --> 00:55:19,659
Why don't they sail back to Ithaca?

1448
00:55:19,659 --> 00:55:21,740
We don't want visitors.

1449
00:55:21,740 --> 00:55:23,368
- But we have to receive them.

1450
00:55:23,368 --> 00:55:25,205
- Well, okay.

1451
00:55:25,205 --> 00:55:27,814
- It would be an offense, a grave offense.

1452
00:55:27,814 --> 00:55:30,558
- And is it not an offense
to me, to be abandoned?

1453
00:55:30,558 --> 00:55:32,601
- Oh, love Herc.

1454
00:55:32,601 --> 00:55:34,434
- I won't be far away.

1455
00:55:35,296 --> 00:55:37,664
I won't be gone long, just time enough

1456
00:55:37,664 --> 00:55:39,032
to pay my respects.

1457
00:55:39,032 --> 00:55:40,617
- And the water bill.

1458
00:55:40,617 --> 00:55:41,852
- Well, it's not everybody
who gets to make out

1459
00:55:41,852 --> 00:55:43,417
at Cypress Gardens.

1460
00:55:43,417 --> 00:55:44,250
- Um-hmm.

1461
00:55:44,250 --> 00:55:45,083
- Wait here.

1462
00:55:45,083 --> 00:55:46,274
I will not be gone.

1463
00:55:46,274 --> 00:55:47,438
- Do I look like I'm going to get up

1464
00:55:47,438 --> 00:55:49,357
and do something?

1465
00:55:49,357 --> 00:55:50,940
- What's for lunch?

1466
00:55:53,890 --> 00:55:57,773
- (clears throat and whistles)

1467
00:55:57,773 --> 00:55:58,750
- Uh-oh.

1468
00:55:58,750 --> 00:56:00,210
- Go on, back to your cell.

1469
00:56:00,210 --> 00:56:01,872
Come on now.

1470
00:56:01,872 --> 00:56:04,917
- Show's over, nothing to see here.

1471
00:56:04,917 --> 00:56:05,750
- Come on.

1472
00:56:06,854 --> 00:56:09,784
- The Aegean Sea has not been
gentle with us, great Queen.

1473
00:56:09,784 --> 00:56:10,886
- I lost it like four times.

1474
00:56:10,886 --> 00:56:13,137
- We have a long perilous
voyage ahead of us.

1475
00:56:13,137 --> 00:56:14,112
- Yeah, boo-hoo.

1476
00:56:14,112 --> 00:56:17,117
- Excuse us, mighty Queen,
since all that you see here

1477
00:56:17,117 --> 00:56:19,483
is poor and modest.

1478
00:56:19,483 --> 00:56:22,849
Mercy and hospitality are all that we ask.

1479
00:56:22,849 --> 00:56:25,767
And these gifts express
our homage and goodwill--

1480
00:56:25,767 --> 00:56:26,600
- These are gifts?

1481
00:56:26,600 --> 00:56:27,840
Don't bother wrapping.

1482
00:56:27,840 --> 00:56:29,215
to you for ruling the island of Lydia--

1483
00:56:29,215 --> 00:56:31,607
- Oh, about the old guy,
he comes with the package.

1484
00:56:31,607 --> 00:56:34,079
- Thank you, Laërtes, King of Ithaca.

1485
00:56:34,079 --> 00:56:35,210
- Hmm.

1486
00:56:35,210 --> 00:56:38,338
- I have already given orders
that you and your friends

1487
00:56:38,338 --> 00:56:41,473
will be taken to the
best wing of the palace.

1488
00:56:41,473 --> 00:56:43,005
- Yeah, by the ice machine.

1489
00:56:43,005 --> 00:56:45,045
- My men will accompany you there.

1490
00:56:45,045 --> 00:56:47,712
- Could your women accompany us?

1491
00:56:50,795 --> 00:56:53,305
- Our humble thank you.

1492
00:56:53,305 --> 00:56:54,714
- I thought our presentation
was pretty good,

1493
00:56:54,714 --> 00:56:56,049
how about you?

1494
00:56:56,049 --> 00:56:57,805
- [Omphale] You, what
is your name, young man?

1495
00:56:57,805 --> 00:57:00,435
- My name is Mrs. Norman Maine.

1496
00:57:00,435 --> 00:57:03,387
- I have the feeling we've
met somewhere before.

1497
00:57:03,387 --> 00:57:05,362
- Oh, I just have the feeling.

1498
00:57:05,362 --> 00:57:07,248
- While the others are
taken to their rooms,

1499
00:57:07,248 --> 00:57:09,081
stay a moment with me.

1500
00:57:11,388 --> 00:57:14,874
I would like to try and
remember where we met.

1501
00:57:14,874 --> 00:57:16,368
- I'm at your service.

1502
00:57:16,368 --> 00:57:19,152
- Oh, she always goes for the jock types.

1503
00:57:19,152 --> 00:57:21,284
- But I am smart, really, and I'm funny.

1504
00:57:21,284 --> 00:57:23,951
Oh, they never pick the old guy.

1505
00:57:26,201 --> 00:57:28,439
- Excuse me, I'm late for my two-thirty.

1506
00:57:28,439 --> 00:57:29,779
- Hercules.

1507
00:57:29,779 --> 00:57:31,019
- What did you say?

1508
00:57:31,019 --> 00:57:32,694
- Hercules?

1509
00:57:32,694 --> 00:57:35,194
- You mean, you don't know me?

1510
00:57:36,881 --> 00:57:38,416
Tell me of Ulysses.

1511
00:57:38,416 --> 00:57:39,275
- Who are you?

1512
00:57:39,275 --> 00:57:40,942
♫ Are you, are you ♫

1513
00:57:40,942 --> 00:57:41,775
- What does this man want from me?

1514
00:57:41,775 --> 00:57:42,608
- Hercules!

1515
00:57:42,608 --> 00:57:44,061
That's not who he is.

1516
00:57:44,061 --> 00:57:45,429
- You're right, Omphale.

1517
00:57:45,429 --> 00:57:47,365
It's just because both
Hercules and this man

1518
00:57:47,365 --> 00:57:48,770
are both gigantic.

1519
00:57:48,770 --> 00:57:50,500
But if you take another look at this man,

1520
00:57:50,500 --> 00:57:52,233
then it's plain to see in a moment

1521
00:57:52,233 --> 00:57:53,817
that we men were in error.

1522
00:57:53,817 --> 00:57:56,570
- I've seen Laërtes, Hercules' face.

1523
00:57:56,570 --> 00:57:57,505
And his figure.

1524
00:57:57,505 --> 00:57:58,906
This couldn't be Hercules.

1525
00:57:58,906 --> 00:58:00,426
- Who is this Hercules?

1526
00:58:00,426 --> 00:58:02,874
- A born fighter and the
greatest man in Thebes.

1527
00:58:02,874 --> 00:58:03,707
A hero.

1528
00:58:03,707 --> 00:58:04,540
- And a hell of an engineer.

1529
00:58:04,540 --> 00:58:05,760
- What does he have to do with me?

1530
00:58:05,760 --> 00:58:06,670
- Nothing.

1531
00:58:06,670 --> 00:58:08,028
Why, it's like water and wine.

1532
00:58:08,028 --> 00:58:08,911
It's bad to mix them.

1533
00:58:08,911 --> 00:58:11,411
- Why is everybody teasing me?

1534
00:58:12,446 --> 00:58:13,279
- Please go.

1535
00:58:13,279 --> 00:58:14,698
I'll see you later.

1536
00:58:14,698 --> 00:58:16,739
- Not later, right this minute.

1537
00:58:16,739 --> 00:58:17,767
- Who are you?

1538
00:58:17,767 --> 00:58:19,559
And who are you?

1539
00:58:19,559 --> 00:58:20,392
Ah!

1540
00:58:21,708 --> 00:58:23,858
- I beg your pardon.

1541
00:58:23,858 --> 00:58:27,368
- Please excuse us, and now
we'll retire, if we may.

1542
00:58:27,368 --> 00:58:31,426
- Oh, here's your gold
watch and your 401k.

1543
00:58:31,426 --> 00:58:33,367
- Miss Utah is a Rhode scholar who wants

1544
00:58:33,367 --> 00:58:36,450
world peace and that special someone.

1545
00:58:41,495 --> 00:58:43,828
- So, live around here much?

1546
00:58:49,559 --> 00:58:51,545
- I want to try this on.

1547
00:58:51,545 --> 00:58:54,545
- What does that have to do with me?

1548
00:58:56,257 --> 00:58:58,957
Pearls must have contact with the flesh

1549
00:58:58,957 --> 00:59:00,915
before they take their best sheen.

1550
00:59:00,915 --> 00:59:03,612
- The closer she gets,
the weirder she looks.

1551
00:59:03,612 --> 00:59:05,013
Ew!

1552
00:59:05,013 --> 00:59:09,355
- This necklace will
be much more beautiful.

1553
00:59:09,355 --> 00:59:10,188
- Well.

1554
00:59:11,622 --> 00:59:13,870
Ah, great sunrise.

1555
00:59:13,870 --> 00:59:15,736
Let's go have breakfast, fellows.

1556
00:59:15,736 --> 00:59:17,819
- It's the old Cedar man.

1557
00:59:21,019 --> 00:59:25,186
- Kind of makes you feel
small, doesn't it, Elvin?

1558
00:59:26,317 --> 00:59:27,484
- Pretty much.

1559
00:59:29,647 --> 00:59:31,271
- Now I'm ready to begin action.

1560
00:59:31,271 --> 00:59:33,316
A man can only live so long patiently.

1561
00:59:33,316 --> 00:59:34,149
- That's nice.

1562
00:59:34,149 --> 00:59:35,940
Ever thought of putting two
similar sentences together?

1563
00:59:35,940 --> 00:59:37,776
- The time is all gone.

1564
00:59:37,776 --> 00:59:39,968
Eteocles and Hercules
are conspiring against me

1565
00:59:39,968 --> 00:59:41,774
in getting the throne.

1566
00:59:41,774 --> 00:59:42,865
- What are you, Jim Garrison?

1567
00:59:42,865 --> 00:59:46,091
- I'll be king yet, and
they, all they need to see

1568
00:59:46,091 --> 00:59:48,029
is this army coming.

1569
00:59:48,029 --> 00:59:49,916
- Your army can sweep under the Thebans.

1570
00:59:49,916 --> 00:59:51,881
- One of the guys has a dustpan head.

1571
00:59:51,881 --> 00:59:54,974
- It'll be a surprise for
my friends down there.

1572
00:59:54,974 --> 00:59:57,414
- Certainly it will be a great
thing, beating the Thebans.

1573
00:59:57,414 --> 00:59:59,551
The throne is there and
the riches of the city.

1574
00:59:59,551 --> 01:00:01,740
- Anything, Mr. Herman.

1575
01:00:01,740 --> 01:00:03,490
- All right. Come on.

1576
01:00:06,342 --> 01:00:07,330
- Bye.

1577
01:00:07,330 --> 01:00:10,330
(suspenseful music)

1578
01:00:13,380 --> 01:00:17,547
