01:19:43,104 --> 01:19:44,086
Drop that ball, drop it!

2102
01:19:44,086 --> 01:19:44,954
Drop it!

2103
01:19:44,954 --> 01:19:46,671
Drop it, drop it!

2104
01:19:46,671 --> 01:19:49,338
(loud growling)

2105
01:19:52,483 --> 01:19:53,829
- Hi, we just thought we'd stop by

2106
01:19:53,829 --> 01:19:55,162
and see what's--

2107
01:19:56,121 --> 01:19:58,788
(loud grunting)

2108
01:20:02,853 --> 01:20:07,020
- Oh, look, it's the Smurfs
versus these kids here.

2109
01:20:10,907 --> 01:20:13,809
- Take your time, Ulysses.

2110
01:20:13,809 --> 01:20:16,476
(loud growling)

2111
01:20:17,409 --> 01:20:18,659
- Aw, boo! Boo!

2112
01:20:20,617 --> 01:20:22,275
- I hate that.

2113
01:20:22,275 --> 01:20:23,775
- He hit Big Jake.

2114
01:20:24,865 --> 01:20:27,532
(loud grunting)

2115
01:20:28,989 --> 01:20:30,906
- Spare the rod, spoil the child.

2116
01:20:30,906 --> 01:20:32,937
Spare the rod and spoil the child.

2117
01:20:32,937 --> 01:20:34,520
- Oh, it says pull.

2118
01:20:35,737 --> 01:20:38,380
(suspenseful music)

2119
01:20:38,380 --> 01:20:40,925
- Look, Herc's got a rip.

2120
01:20:40,925 --> 01:20:43,277
(suspenseful music)

2121
01:20:43,277 --> 01:20:44,110
(loud crash)

2122
01:20:44,110 --> 01:20:46,020
- Knock, knock! Ha!

2123
01:20:46,020 --> 01:20:48,603
(upbeat music)

2124
01:20:50,964 --> 01:20:52,788
(suspenseful music)

2125
01:20:52,788 --> 01:20:54,671
- Gee, you know, if somebody
had invented boxing,

2126
01:20:54,671 --> 01:20:57,807
They'd save a lot of time here.

2127
01:20:57,807 --> 01:21:00,291
(loud clanging)

2128
01:21:00,291 --> 01:21:01,208
- Oh, look!

2129
01:21:02,685 --> 01:21:03,518
- Do you want to go?

2130
01:21:03,518 --> 01:21:05,703
- Yeah, sure. Your place?

2131
01:21:05,703 --> 01:21:08,536
(horses neighing)

2132
01:21:11,134 --> 01:21:12,949
- Oh, I'll be right back.

2133
01:21:12,949 --> 01:21:13,999
I forgot something.

2134
01:21:13,999 --> 01:21:17,058
I'll catch you in the flip flop, okay?

2135
01:21:17,058 --> 01:21:19,648
(loud cheer)

2136
01:21:19,648 --> 01:21:23,193
- Now, it's just me and you, mano a mano.

2137
01:21:23,193 --> 01:21:25,285
- Tonight it's Abe Agoda
versus James Whitmore

2138
01:21:25,285 --> 01:21:27,738
in a battle to the death.

2139
01:21:27,738 --> 01:21:31,205
(loud clanging)

2140
01:21:31,205 --> 01:21:35,594
- You know, there's no bad
seats in this stadium, huh?

2141
01:21:35,594 --> 01:21:37,995
- You know, I was just
wondering where Hercules went.

2142
01:21:37,995 --> 01:21:39,753
- I wonder where the movie went.

2143
01:21:39,753 --> 01:21:42,420
(loud clanging)

2144
01:21:44,191 --> 01:21:45,121
- Oh!

2145
01:21:45,121 --> 01:21:48,058
- Oh, you cut me, you jerk!

2146
01:21:48,058 --> 01:21:50,788
- Hello, my name is Inigo Montoya.

2147
01:21:50,788 --> 01:21:51,903
You killed my father.

2148
01:21:51,903 --> 01:21:53,153
Prepare to die.

2149
01:21:55,432 --> 01:21:58,924
- And fighting over who
had that hairstyle first.

2150
01:21:58,924 --> 01:22:00,048
- I look like Lucille!

2151
01:22:00,048 --> 01:22:02,215
- No, I look like Lucille!

2152
01:22:03,347 --> 01:22:05,584
(crying out)

2153
01:22:05,584 --> 01:22:08,548
- Now he's the knight of
the living dead (chuckles).

2154
01:22:08,548 --> 01:22:09,903
- Ooh.

2155
01:22:09,903 --> 01:22:11,187
(maniacal laughter)

2156
01:22:11,187 --> 01:22:15,020
- This guy finds the
funny side of everything.

2157
01:22:19,659 --> 01:22:20,492
- Thank you.

2158
01:22:20,492 --> 01:22:21,588
Now, for my next trick, I need a volunteer

2159
01:22:21,588 --> 01:22:22,421
from the audience.

2160
01:22:22,421 --> 01:22:26,004
- Thebans, pray to the
gods because at last

2161
01:22:27,794 --> 01:22:29,794
Eteocles has won the day

2162
01:22:32,491 --> 01:22:33,991
and is victorious!

2163
01:22:39,480 --> 01:22:40,909
- He's no fun.

2164
01:22:40,909 --> 01:22:42,492
He fell right over.

2165
01:22:43,420 --> 01:22:44,919
- What a letdown.

2166
01:22:44,919 --> 01:22:45,752
- Aw.

2167
01:22:46,631 --> 01:22:48,298
- And now, a prayer.

2168
01:22:50,225 --> 01:22:52,528
- Now, I suppose I've got to go clean up,

2169
01:22:52,528 --> 01:22:54,195
for crying out loud.

2170
01:22:57,209 --> 01:22:59,205
(horse neighing)

2171
01:22:59,205 --> 01:23:02,591
I know, I feel the same way, horse.

2172
01:23:02,591 --> 01:23:03,627
- Come on, get up.

2173
01:23:03,627 --> 01:23:06,294
Still gotta go to school, dummy.

2174
01:23:10,288 --> 01:23:12,151
- The redhead is dead.

2175
01:23:12,151 --> 01:23:14,092
- He was as stupid as his brother.

2176
01:23:14,092 --> 01:23:15,501
They deserve to end this way.

2177
01:23:15,501 --> 01:23:17,908
- He learned too late that
man is a feeling creature,

2178
01:23:17,908 --> 01:23:19,788
and because of it, the
greatest in the universe.

2179
01:23:19,788 --> 01:23:21,427
He learned too late for himself that men

2180
01:23:21,427 --> 01:23:22,845
have to make their own way and--

2181
01:23:22,845 --> 01:23:24,640
- Yeah, yeah.

2182
01:23:24,640 --> 01:23:27,532
- Hercules, do you see this?

2183
01:23:27,532 --> 01:23:29,281
Well, I shall celebrate this victory.

2184
01:23:29,281 --> 01:23:32,204
She's in my house now,
and I'm going there.

2185
01:23:32,204 --> 01:23:34,235
- And I've got cable!

2186
01:23:34,235 --> 01:23:36,757
- Uh, what time should I come over?

2187
01:23:36,757 --> 01:23:38,318
Do you want me to bring something?

2188
01:23:38,318 --> 01:23:39,629
- Get to your posts!

2189
01:23:39,629 --> 01:23:41,528
- Get my purse?

2190
01:23:41,528 --> 01:23:44,528
(suspenseful music)

2191
01:23:46,175 --> 01:23:47,202
- You know, this is like I, Claudius,

2192
01:23:47,202 --> 01:23:49,279
only it's not good at all.

2193
01:23:49,279 --> 01:23:52,464
(suspenseful music)

2194
01:23:52,464 --> 01:23:54,077
- You know, they really are talented.

2195
01:23:54,077 --> 01:23:56,278
They put on such a great show, you know.

2196
01:23:56,278 --> 01:23:59,240
They give 110% over there, you know.

2197
01:23:59,240 --> 01:24:00,742
- Oh, yeah.

2198
01:24:00,742 --> 01:24:01,659
- Oh, yeah.

2199
01:24:02,591 --> 01:24:06,227
- Let's break off and start another movie!

2200
01:24:06,227 --> 01:24:07,060
- Ha, look.

2201
01:24:07,060 --> 01:24:07,986
It looks like they've
got the leftover parts

2202
01:24:07,986 --> 01:24:10,611
from an airplane model.

2203
01:24:10,611 --> 01:24:14,053
- It's the world's largest chess set.

2204
01:24:14,053 --> 01:24:16,850
- It's a traveling rest stop.

2205
01:24:16,850 --> 01:24:21,508
♫ Du du dum, dum dum ♫

2206
01:24:21,508 --> 01:24:22,825
- Why, look at that.

2207
01:24:22,825 --> 01:24:24,903
The Thebans are abandoning their defenses.

2208
01:24:24,903 --> 01:24:26,103
- Oh, do you see that?

2209
01:24:26,103 --> 01:24:27,743
- They must be surrendering the town.

2210
01:24:27,743 --> 01:24:31,910
- Looks like they brought the
whole darn town with them!

2211
01:24:33,927 --> 01:24:36,229
- It's Ted Koppel's head, look out!

2212
01:24:36,229 --> 01:24:37,146
- Ooh! Aah!

2213
01:24:42,918 --> 01:24:45,609
- Hey, come on and
interrupt, you gladiators!

2214
01:24:45,609 --> 01:24:48,274
- Ladies and gentlemen, Elvis Presley!

2215
01:24:48,274 --> 01:24:51,607
(imitating funky music)

2216
01:24:53,526 --> 01:24:55,973
- And each float is made of 75,000

2217
01:24:55,973 --> 01:24:59,140
individual fresh flowers put in place.

2218
01:25:01,694 --> 01:25:03,771
- Yup, I'm the title character.

2219
01:25:03,771 --> 01:25:05,189
That's me, pretty much.

2220
01:25:05,189 --> 01:25:07,022
Herc, your friend, hi.

2221
01:25:08,440 --> 01:25:11,811
(suspenseful music)

2222
01:25:11,811 --> 01:25:12,821
- Hey, does anybody have an idea

2223
01:25:12,821 --> 01:25:13,957
what we're doing here?

2224
01:25:13,957 --> 01:25:15,039
- I thought you knew!

2225
01:25:15,039 --> 01:25:16,198
- No!

2226
01:25:16,198 --> 01:25:19,198
(suspenseful music)

2227
01:25:29,938 --> 01:25:31,913
- Oh, thank you.

2228
01:25:31,913 --> 01:25:34,525
- This kind of reminds me
of The Empire Strikes Back,

2229
01:25:34,525 --> 01:25:35,909
except it's not very good.

2230
01:25:35,909 --> 01:25:37,125
- Yeah, not really.

2231
01:25:37,125 --> 01:25:39,503
(horses neighing)

2232
01:25:39,503 --> 01:25:40,336
- Oh!

2233
01:25:43,088 --> 01:25:44,864
♫ Pum pum pududum pum pum pum pum

2234
01:25:44,864 --> 01:25:49,051
♫ Pum dududum dum du ♫

2235
01:25:49,051 --> 01:25:50,002
(loud screaming)

2236
01:25:50,002 --> 01:25:52,247
- Hercules, those are our guys, you idiot!

2237
01:25:52,247 --> 01:25:55,247
(suspenseful music)

2238
01:25:59,725 --> 01:26:02,050
- Oh, now here comes the Boston marathon!

2239
01:26:02,050 --> 01:26:03,594
- Forward the cavalry!

2240
01:26:03,594 --> 01:26:05,764
- That's not my department,
Captain Reynolds!

2241
01:26:05,764 --> 01:26:08,200
- Yeah, yeah, I know.

2242
01:26:08,200 --> 01:26:11,200
Once more, under the breach, I know.

2243
01:26:12,101 --> 01:26:13,407
(horses neighing)

2244
01:26:13,407 --> 01:26:14,240
- Boo!

2245
01:26:14,240 --> 01:26:15,073
- I hate this!

2246
01:26:15,073 --> 01:26:15,906
- I'm calling Betty White.

2247
01:26:15,906 --> 01:26:16,739
- And I'm calling Tippi Hedron.

2248
01:26:16,739 --> 01:26:19,268
- And I'm calling Brigitte Bardot.

2249
01:26:19,268 --> 01:26:23,435
- Black Beauty, Flicka, Scout,
Trigger, Secretariat, no!

2250
01:26:25,277 --> 01:26:28,300
- It's like the end of
the Mel Brooks movie.

2251
01:26:28,300 --> 01:26:30,276
(horses neighing)

2252
01:26:30,276 --> 01:26:32,350
(loud screaming)

2253
01:26:32,350 --> 01:26:34,393
- Oo-hoo, that's good tower.

2254
01:26:34,393 --> 01:26:35,393
- Checkmate.

2255
01:26:37,838 --> 01:26:41,421
- Oh, look at the
Sisters of Saint Francis.

2256
01:26:43,343 --> 01:26:45,632
- Last day of school is always like this.

2257
01:26:45,632 --> 01:26:46,465
- Nutty.

2258
01:26:49,785 --> 01:26:51,535
- And die, thank you.

2259
01:26:52,844 --> 01:26:54,353
- Okay, everybody, off the set.

2260
01:26:54,353 --> 01:26:56,025
We're trying to clear the
set for the end of the movie.

2261
01:26:56,025 --> 01:26:59,025
Please leave the set now, thank you.

2262
01:27:00,589 --> 01:27:03,176
- Buh-bye! (chuckles)

2263
01:27:03,176 --> 01:27:04,009
- Bye now.

2264
01:27:06,086 --> 01:27:07,445
- Epilogue.

2265
01:27:07,445 --> 01:27:08,776
- Spalding Gray?

2266
01:27:08,776 --> 01:27:12,995
- The Thebes took revenge
on Oedipus and his sons too.

2267
01:27:12,995 --> 01:27:15,821
- And his friend Chopper is real fun.

2268
01:27:15,821 --> 01:27:18,105
- For inciting the gods.

2269
01:27:18,105 --> 01:27:19,918
Now with these flames,
they purify our city

2270
01:27:19,918 --> 01:27:22,170
and those who shall stay.

2271
01:27:22,170 --> 01:27:24,464
- Or something like that, I think.

2272
01:27:24,464 --> 01:27:25,297
You'll have to excuse me.

2273
01:27:25,297 --> 01:27:26,964
I'm really hungover.

2274
01:27:29,851 --> 01:27:32,277
- Oh, honey, about all
that boinking and boinking

2275
01:27:32,277 --> 01:27:35,515
that I did on the island,
well, it's nothing.

2276
01:27:35,515 --> 01:27:37,642
- How much you've suffered, Iole.

2277
01:27:37,642 --> 01:27:40,636
The gods have placed many
obstacles against us,

2278
01:27:40,636 --> 01:27:41,803
and there will be others.

2279
01:27:41,803 --> 01:27:43,619
- Yeah, well, you're
sleeping on the couch, Herc.

2280
01:27:43,619 --> 01:27:45,645
- I hope we shall withstand.

2281
01:27:45,645 --> 01:27:49,386
Somehow the gods will be kind
if we just love one another.

2282
01:27:49,386 --> 01:27:51,711
- Are they in heaven?

2283
01:27:51,711 --> 01:27:55,211
- Now, Herc, no more business trips, okay?

2284
01:27:56,226 --> 01:27:58,708
- This is the end of the
story of forgetfulness.

2285
01:27:58,708 --> 01:28:01,441
Those who watch of it will die of boredom.

2286
01:28:01,441 --> 01:28:02,274
Ah!

2287
01:28:04,670 --> 01:28:05,587
Mm, stinky.

2288
01:28:11,829 --> 01:28:14,746
(mechanical noise)

2289
01:28:20,698 --> 01:28:22,650
- Hey, Joelster, why these kind of movies?

2290
01:28:22,650 --> 01:28:24,150
- Well, that's a good question, Gypsy.

2291
01:28:24,150 --> 01:28:26,131
However, there aren't any simple answers.

2292
01:28:26,131 --> 01:28:27,618
- Well, yes, there are.

2293
01:28:27,618 --> 01:28:29,169
- I think maybe it's a cultural thing.

2294
01:28:29,169 --> 01:28:30,787
You know, the post-war era.

2295
01:28:30,787 --> 01:28:32,986
- Right, that's exactly right, Crow.

2296
01:28:32,986 --> 01:28:35,560
You know, western culture had a real need

2297
01:28:35,560 --> 01:28:38,730
during the Cold War for
a fantastic spectacle.

2298
01:28:38,730 --> 01:28:40,125
- Yeah, spectacles!

2299
01:28:40,125 --> 01:28:40,958
- Yeah, it's true.

2300
01:28:40,958 --> 01:28:43,361
After Liz Taylor accepted
over a million dollars

2301
01:28:43,361 --> 01:28:45,429
for a role in Cleopatra, you know,

2302
01:28:45,429 --> 01:28:48,135
big-budget blockbusters
became the coin of the realm.

2303
01:28:48,135 --> 01:28:49,802
- No, wrong, guys, wrong.

2304
01:28:49,802 --> 01:28:51,196
- I was thinking more along the lines

2305
01:28:51,196 --> 01:28:53,861
of European indignation
towards post-war conservatism

2306
01:28:53,861 --> 01:28:56,293
and sexual repression which translated

2307
01:28:56,293 --> 01:28:58,236
onto the screen in the big sweaty guys

2308
01:28:58,236 --> 01:28:59,594
pushing girls around.

2309
01:28:59,594 --> 01:29:01,177
- Crow, you are so high.

2310
01:29:01,177 --> 01:29:02,010
- No, come on.

2311
01:29:02,010 --> 01:29:03,195
Crow's got a point.

2312
01:29:03,195 --> 01:29:05,505
Without sex, would Hercules Unchained

2313
01:29:05,505 --> 01:29:06,709
have even been made?

2314
01:29:06,709 --> 01:29:08,507
- Joseph Campbell.

2315
01:29:08,507 --> 01:29:09,684
- Huh?

2316
01:29:09,684 --> 01:29:10,861
- Joseph Campbell?

2317
01:29:10,861 --> 01:29:14,109
- Oh, I think what our bright young friend

2318
01:29:14,109 --> 01:29:17,935
is trying to remind us of is
the need for myth, you know,

2319
01:29:17,935 --> 01:29:19,575
the collective dream.

2320
01:29:19,575 --> 01:29:20,408
- Oh, yeah, yeah.

2321
01:29:20,408 --> 01:29:21,710
There's a need for gods and heroes.

2322
01:29:21,710 --> 01:29:23,387
I remember that Joseph
Campbell said something

2323
01:29:23,387 --> 01:29:26,762
in one of those books of his with masks

2324
01:29:26,762 --> 01:29:30,004
and stuff in it, and that this thing

2325
01:29:30,004 --> 01:29:31,530
you're supposed to do.

2326
01:29:31,530 --> 01:29:32,757
- Wrong, wrong.

2327
01:29:32,757 --> 01:29:34,483
- Come on, I think we can probe deeper

2328
01:29:34,483 --> 01:29:36,119
into the phenomenal--

2329
01:29:36,119 --> 01:29:37,702
- Phenomenological.

2330
01:29:38,954 --> 01:29:39,787
- Yeah.

2331
01:29:39,787 --> 01:29:42,729
I think we can probe deeper
into the phenomenological basis

2332
01:29:42,729 --> 01:29:44,614
for a Hercules experience.

2333
01:29:44,614 --> 01:29:47,192
- Discarding the classical
dualistic view, of course.

2334
01:29:47,192 --> 01:29:48,711
- How do you figure?

2335
01:29:48,711 --> 01:29:50,864
- Well, Gypsy, every phenomenon belongs

2336
01:29:50,864 --> 01:29:54,195
to a regional anthology
by virtue of its essence.

2337
01:29:54,195 --> 01:29:55,979
- Look, I'll make it easy for all of you!

2338
01:29:55,979 --> 01:29:57,699
Joseph E. Levine picked these turkeys up

2339
01:29:57,699 --> 01:30:00,125
after a sagging European
box drove the price

2340
01:30:00,125 --> 01:30:02,324
way down that he dumped
right into America,

2341
01:30:02,324 --> 01:30:03,824
then amassed a distribution deal,

2342
01:30:03,824 --> 01:30:05,220
and made a fortune, okay?

2343
01:30:05,220 --> 01:30:07,148
- You're wrong.

2344
01:30:07,148 --> 01:30:08,140
- Oh.

2345
01:30:08,140 --> 01:30:09,172
- Philistine.

2346
01:30:09,172 --> 01:30:10,005
- Tom.

2347
01:30:10,005 --> 01:30:11,370
- Well, well, it's true.

2348
01:30:11,370 --> 01:30:12,203
Am I right, sirs?

2349
01:30:12,203 --> 01:30:14,536
Come on, back me up on this.

2350
01:30:15,547 --> 01:30:16,590
- Yeah.

2351
01:30:16,590 --> 01:30:20,128
- Oh, well, Steve, is that right?

2352
01:30:20,128 --> 01:30:20,961
- Huh?

2353
01:30:21,998 --> 01:30:23,291
Yeah, I guess so.

2354
01:30:23,291 --> 01:30:24,512
I mean, there are these guys in suits

2355
01:30:24,512 --> 01:30:26,270
that used to drive up the coast

2356
01:30:26,270 --> 01:30:28,214
and check on us every now and then.

2357
01:30:28,214 --> 01:30:29,917
I didn't really get to meet them much.

2358
01:30:29,917 --> 01:30:31,562
I was usually up on the cliff,

2359
